window.GLOWSIS_BOOK = [{"id":0,"sections":[{"cls":"unit-flag","html":"<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 0 · PREPARATION</div>\n  "},{"cls":"sec-title","html":"<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">0</div><div><h2>Hangul First Steps</h2><div class=\"en\">한글 — the ABC of Korean</div></div></div>\n\n  <!-- 한글의 비밀 — 상세 시리즈 -->\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">📜 The Secret of Hangul ① — The Story of Hunminjeongeum</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">A letter created by King Sejong for the people</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Long ago, Koreans used Chinese characters (한자). But hanja was so hard that <b>common people could neither read nor write.</b> King Sejong said, \"The people suffer because they cannot write down what they want to say,\" and created <b>a new alphabet anyone could learn easily.</b> Its name is <b>Hunminjeongeum (훈민정음)</b> — meaning \"the correct sounds for teaching the people.\"</div>\n    <div class=\"h-timeline\">\n      <div class=\"ht-item\"><span class=\"ht-year\">1443</span><span class=\"ht-text\">King Sejong <b>created</b> Hunminjeongeum (28 letters).</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ht-item\"><span class=\"ht-year\">1446</span><span class=\"ht-text\">Published as the <b>Hunminjeongeum Haerye</b> — released to the world with its principle manual.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ht-item\"><span class=\"ht-year\">1910s</span><span class=\"ht-text\">Scholar Ju Si-gyeong named it <b>Hangul</b> — meaning \"the great and correct script.\"</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ht-item\"><span class=\"ht-year\">오늘</span><span class=\"ht-text\">With 24 letters (14 consonants + 10 vowels), it is recognized as <b>the world's most scientific writing system.</b></span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">🔤 The Secret of Hangul ② — Consonants are \"Shapes of the Mouth\"!</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">Consonants made by imitating the shape of the speech organs</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">The 5 basic consonants were made by copying the <b>shape of the mouth, tongue, and throat as they move when you speak.</b> Just looking at the letter shows you how to pronounce it!</div>\n    <div class=\"hangul-grid\">\n      <div class=\"h-cell highlight\"><div class=\"h-jamo\">ㄱ</div><div class=\"h-rom\">g/k</div><div class=\"h-name\">기역</div><div class=\"h-desc\">Shape of the tongue root blocking the throat</div></div>\n      <div class=\"h-cell highlight\"><div class=\"h-jamo\">ㄴ</div><div class=\"h-rom\">n</div><div class=\"h-name\">니은</div><div class=\"h-desc\">Shape of the tongue tip touching the upper gum</div></div>\n      <div class=\"h-cell highlight\"><div class=\"h-jamo\">ㅁ</div><div class=\"h-rom\">m</div><div class=\"h-name\">미음</div><div class=\"h-desc\">Shape of pursed lips</div></div>\n      <div class=\"h-cell highlight\"><div class=\"h-jamo\">ㅅ</div><div class=\"h-rom\">s</div><div class=\"h-name\">시옷</div><div class=\"h-desc\">Shape of the teeth</div></div>\n      <div class=\"h-cell highlight\"><div class=\"h-jamo\">ㅇ</div><div class=\"h-rom\">ng</div><div class=\"h-name\">이응</div><div class=\"h-desc\">Shape of the throat</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Add a stroke and it becomes a <b>stronger sound</b>: ㄱ→ㅋ, ㄴ→ㄷ→ㅌ, ㅁ→ㅂ→ㅍ, ㅅ→ㅈ→ㅊ. <b>One extra stroke = one stronger sound!</b></div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">🌌 The Secret of Hangul ③ — Vowels are \"Heaven, Earth, Human\"!</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">Cheonji-in (天地人) — vowels that draw the universe</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Vowels are made from just <b>three symbols</b>: <b>ㆍ (heaven, a dot)</b> · <b>ㅡ (earth, something flat)</b> · <b>ㅣ (human, a standing figure)</b>. Every vowel is born from how these three are arranged!</div>\n    <div class=\"hangul-grid\">\n      <div class=\"h-cell\"><div class=\"h-jamo\">ㆍ</div><div class=\"h-rom\">(arae-a)</div><div class=\"h-name\">하늘</div><div class=\"h-desc\">Round dot = heaven</div></div>\n      <div class=\"h-cell\"><div class=\"h-jamo\">ㅡ</div><div class=\"h-rom\">eu</div><div class=\"h-name\">땅</div><div class=\"h-desc\">Flat earth</div></div>\n      <div class=\"h-cell\"><div class=\"h-jamo\">ㅣ</div><div class=\"h-rom\">i</div><div class=\"h-name\">사람</div><div class=\"h-desc\">Standing person</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">The combination rule:</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">ㅣ + ㆍ = ㅏ / ㅓ</span><span class=\"gl\">Heaven (ㆍ) to the right of human (ㅣ) → ㅏ · to the left → ㅓ</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">ㅡ + ㆍ = ㅗ / ㅜ</span><span class=\"gl\">Heaven above earth (ㅡ) → ㅗ · below → ㅜ</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">ㅏ + ㅣ = ㅐ / ㅔ</span><span class=\"gl\">When vowels combine, a new vowel is born!</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">🧱 The Secret of Hangul ④ — One letter = one syllable block</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">Consonant + vowel come together to form \"one letter\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Hangul is not written in a row like the alphabet. Instead, <b>consonants and vowels are stacked in one block</b> to form one syllable. You can even add a final consonant (받침) below!</div>\n    <div class=\"h-block-demo\">\n      <div class=\"h-block\"><div class=\"hb-main\">가</div><div class=\"hb-sub\">ㄱ + ㅏ</div></div>\n      <div class=\"h-block-op\">→</div>\n      <div class=\"h-block\"><div class=\"hb-main\">간</div><div class=\"hb-sub\">ㄱ + ㅏ + ㄴ</div></div>\n      <div class=\"h-block-op\">→</div>\n      <div class=\"h-block\"><div class=\"hb-main\">사랑</div><div class=\"hb-sub\">사 + 랑 · 2 blocks</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Stack blocks to make words, then sentences! Example: <b>사랑해요</b> = 사 + 랑 + 해 + 요 (4 blocks)</div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">🏆 The Secret of Hangul ⑤ — A Script Recognized by the World</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">\"The most remarkable writing system on Earth\" — world linguists</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Hunminjeongeum is registered as a <b>UNESCO Memory of the World</b>. American linguist Edwin Reischauer praised it as <b>\"the finest writing system in the world.\"</b> Because sound and letter map 1:1, it is easy to learn!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">한글날 — 10월 9일</span><span class=\"gl\">A Korean national holiday celebrating Hangul!</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">유네스코 세계기록유산 (1997)</span><span class=\"gl\">Hunminjeongeum Haerye registered</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">훈민정음 → 한글</span><span class=\"gl\">Today's name was given by Ju Si-gyeong</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">🎵 Reading Hangul through K-pop Group Names</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">The group names you love — this is how they are written in Korean!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Foreign words are written in Hangul by their sound. Let's read K-pop group names together!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">BTS → 비티에스</span><span class=\"gl\">bi-ti-e-seu · 방탄소년단 (Bulletproof Boy Scouts)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">BLACKPINK → 블랙핑크</span><span class=\"gl\">beul-laek-ping-keu</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">TWICE → 트와이스</span><span class=\"gl\">teu-wa-i-seu</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">NEWJEANS → 뉴진스</span><span class=\"gl\">nyu-jin-seu</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">글로시스 → GLOWSIS</span><span class=\"gl\">Our group's name! Glow(빛나다) + Sis(언니) = 빛나는 언니들 ✨</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n    <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-1] Hangul Sound Match</span></div>\n    <div class=\"p-dir\">Read the Hangul word and choose the correct pronunciation. 🔊 Press the button to hear the sound.</div>\n    <div class=\"p-q\">Read and choose the correct answer. — <span class=\"blank\">뉴진스</span></div>\n    <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u0q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u0q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> nu-jin-seu<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u0q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> nyu-jin-seu<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 뉴 = nyu</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u0q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> niu-jin-seu<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u0q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> nu-jin-ssu<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div>\n    <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u0q1\"></div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n    <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-2] Group Names in Hangul</span></div>\n    <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct Hangul spelling.</div>\n    <div class=\"p-q\">Read and choose the correct answer. — <b>How do you write \"TWICE\" in Hangul?</b></div>\n    <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u0q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u0q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 트바이스<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u0q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 트와이스<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u0q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 트웨이스<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u0q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 트아이스<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div>\n    <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u0q2\"></div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"culture","html":"<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>How to Call an Idol</h3>\n    <p>In Korea, you add <b>씨</b> after an idol's name. Fans also call them <b>오빠/언니/누나/형</b>!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">💜 아란 씨, 사랑해요! (Aran, I love you!) — You'll learn cheering phrases in Unit 1.</div>\n  </div>\n\n<!-- ============================================================\n     UNIT 1 — GREETINGS\n     ============================================================ -->"}]},{"id":1,"sections":[{"cls":"unit-flag","html":"<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 1 · GREETINGS</div>\n  "},{"cls":"sec-title","html":"<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">1</div><div><h2>Hello!</h2><div class=\"en\">안녕하세요! — Greetings & 이에요/예요</div></div></div>\n  "},{"cls":"story","html":"<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/story/u1.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 1/8</span>\n      <h3>아란, 첫 번째 안녕 — \"안녕하세요!\"</h3>\n      <p>글로시스의 첫 연습실! 리더 <b>아란</b>은 한국어로 인사하는 법을 배워요. \"안녕하세요\"라는 말에 팬들의 마음이 열려요. ⭐</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">It's Glowsis's very first practice room! Leader <b>Aran</b> learns how to greet people in Korean. With the word \"안녕하세요\" (Hello), fans' hearts open wide. ⭐</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">⭐ GLOW POINT 1/8 획득 — Greetings!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"goals","html":"<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">👋</span> Learn greeting expressions</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🔤</span> N은/는 N이에요/예요</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🎤</span> Idol greeting phrases</div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"dialog","html":"<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 1 — First Meeting</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🏢 First day at the practice room</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">안녕하세요! 저는 아란이에요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Hello! I'm Aran.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">안녕하세요! 저는 다희예요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Hello! I'm Dahee.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">안녕하세요? 저는 로이예요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Hello? I'm Roy.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">만나서 반가워요! 저는 로이예요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Nice to meet you! I'm Roy.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">N은/는 N이에요/예요</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">\"A is B\" — use it to introduce yourself. If the noun ends with a final consonant (받침), use <b>이에요</b>; otherwise use <b>예요</b>.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 아란<b>이에요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">아란 ends with ㄴ (final consonant) → 이에요</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 로이<b>예요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">로이 ends with ㅣ (no final consonant) → 예요</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 가수<b>예요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I am a singer.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">Greetings</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">These greetings always appear in the TOPIK I listening section.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">안녕하세요!</span><span class=\"gl\">Hello! / Good morning!</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">만나서 반가워요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Nice to meet you.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">안녕히 가세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Goodbye (to someone leaving).</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">안녕히 계세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Goodbye (said by the one leaving).</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">감사합니다!</span><span class=\"gl\">Thank you!</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n    "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">N입니다 / N입니까? — Formal polite form</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">More formal than 이에요/예요 — used in news, announcements, and stage greetings. <b>입니다</b> = statement, <b>입니까?</b> = question.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">안녕하세요, 글로시스입니다!</span><span class=\"gl\">Hello, we are Glowsis! (stage greeting)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">학생입니까?</span><span class=\"gl\">Are you a student?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">네, 학생입니다.</span><span class=\"gl\">Yes, I am a student.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"},{"cls":"teach","html":"<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · 이에요 vs 예요 + 저는</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 가수예요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"I am a singer.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Why is it <b>예요</b> and not <b>이에요</b> after 가수 — and what is 저는 doing at the very front?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      Korean ends many words with a <b>final consonant (받침)</b> — a consonant that sits underneath the last syllable. To say \"is,\" Korean uses <b>이다</b>. But a bare <b>에요</b> needs a vowel right before it to glide on. So after a final consonant we <b>plug in an extra 이</b> and say <b>이에요</b>; after a plain vowel we <b>drop the 이</b> and just say <b>예요</b>. <b class=\"hl\">가수</b> (\"singer\") ends in the vowel ㅜ and has <b>no 받침</b>, so it takes <b>예요</b>: 저는 가수예요. And <b class=\"hl\">저는</b> = \"as for me\" — 저 is the polite word for \"I,\" and the particle 는 marks it as the topic.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">저</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">I <span class=\"t-sub\">(polite \"me\")</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Humble word for \"I,\"<br>used with new people &amp; on stage.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">는</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">topic particle</div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">\"as for me\" — marks<br>저 as what we're talking about.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">가수</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">singer <span class=\"t-sub\">(vowel ㅜ)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">No 받침 at the end,<br>so the next word is 예요.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">예요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">= is <span class=\"t-sub\">(이다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">가수<b>예요</b> = 가수<b>이에요</b>.<br>After a vowel we say just 예요.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">저는 가수예요.</b> = \"As for me, (I) am a singer.\" The 받침 decides the ending: a word that <b>ends in a consonant</b> (like <b>아란</b> → ㄴ) gets <b>이에요</b>, while a word that <b>ends in a vowel</b> (like <b>가수</b> → ㅜ) gets <b>예요</b>. The 이 is like a <b>bridge</b> that carries the ending across a final consonant so it stays easy to pronounce.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Has 받침 → 이에요</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 아란<b>이에요</b>.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">아란 ends with ㄴ (consonant)</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>No 받침 → 예요</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 가수<b>예요</b>.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">가수 ends with ㅜ (vowel)</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> If the last letter has a 받침 (a consonant \"cap\" under it), say <b>이에요</b>. If the last letter is an open vowel, say <b>예요</b>. Greeting trick: <b>안녕하세요!</b> opens the talk, then <b>저는 …예요</b> tells who you are — that's the whole first-meeting formula.\n  </div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"vocab-lab","html":"<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🧑🎤</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">사람 & 아이돌<small>저/이름/가수/친구/팬</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">5</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u1_me.webp\" alt=\"저\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">저</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jeo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">I (polite)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u1_nametag.webp\" alt=\"이름\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이름')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">이름</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ireum</div><div class=\"vw-en\">name</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u1_singer.webp\" alt=\"가수\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가수')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">가수</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gasu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">singer</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u1_friend.webp\" alt=\"친구\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('친구')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">친구</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chingu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">friend</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u1_fan.webp\" alt=\"팬\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('팬')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">팬</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">paen</div><div class=\"vw-en\">fan</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 가수예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 가수예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I am a singer.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('제 이름은 아란이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">제 이름은 아란이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">My name is Aran.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가수는 노래를 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">가수는 노래를 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">A singer sings songs.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('우리는 좋은 친구예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">우리는 좋은 친구예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We are good friends.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 아란의 팬이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 아란의 팬이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I am Aran's fan.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🤝 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> 저는 <b>이름을 말할 때</b>, 팬은 <b>가수의 노래</b>를 좋아해요. 가수와 팬은 <b>친구</b>처럼 지내요!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎤</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">무대 & 음악<small>노래/무대</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u1_song.webp\" alt=\"노래\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('노래')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">노래</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">norae</div><div class=\"vw-en\">song</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u1_stage.webp\" alt=\"무대\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('무대')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">무대</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">mudae</div><div class=\"vw-en\">stage</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('글로시스는 무대에서 노래해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">글로시스는 무대에서 노래해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Glowsis sings on stage.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 노래는 무대에서 불러요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 노래는 무대에서 불러요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We sing this song on stage.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 글로시스 노래를 좋아해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 글로시스 노래를 좋아해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I like Glowsis songs.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🎶 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> 가수는 <b>무대에서</b> <b>노래해요</b>. 무대(舞台) = stage, 노래 = song — 들리는 말끝 <b>-예요/-이에요</b>와 함께 자주 나와요!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">👋</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">인사말<small>안녕/감사합니다</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u1_hi.webp\" alt=\"안녕\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('안녕')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">안녕</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">annyeong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">hi / bye (informal)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u1_thanks.webp\" alt=\"감사합니다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('감사합니다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">감사합니다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gamsahamnida</div><div class=\"vw-en\">thank you</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('안녕하세요! 저는 아란이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">안녕하세요! 저는 아란이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Hello! I am Aran.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('안녕! 오랜만이야.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">안녕! 오랜만이야.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Hi! Long time no see. (informal)</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('노래 감사합니다!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">노래 감사합니다!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Thank you for the song!</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🤲 <b>둘 다 인사예요:</b> 안녕은 친한 사이의 <b>인사말</b>, 감사합니다는 <b>고마울 때</b> 써요. 무대 끝나면 팬들에게 “<b>감사합니다!</b>” 하고 인사해요!</div></div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-1] Reading — 받침 — 저는 가수예요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct ending to complete the sentence: \"I am a singer.\"</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 가수(     ).</span> <span class=\"gl\">(singer = 가수)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u1q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>예요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 가수 ends in the vowel ㅜ, no 받침 → 예요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>이에요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ needs a final consonant</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>이어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not a real form here</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ = \"have / exist\"</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u1q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">가수</b> (\"singer\") ends in the vowel <b class=\"hl\">ㅜ</b> — no 받침 — so it takes <b class=\"hl\">예요</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">이에요</b> is only for words with a final consonant (아란→아란이에요); <b class=\"hl\">있어요</b> means \"to have / exist,\" not \"is.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 No 받침 = <span class=\"pt-ko\">예요</span>. Final consonant = <span class=\"pt-ko\">이에요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-2] Reading — Vocab — 이름</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read the question and choose what it means.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">이름이 뭐예요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u1q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>What is that?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 이거 뭐예요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>What is your name?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 이름 = \"name\"; 뭐 = what</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>How old are you?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ a different question</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>Where are you from?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ a different question</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u1q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">이름</span> means <b class=\"hl\">\"name.\"</b> So <span class=\"pt-ko\">이름이 뭐예요?</span> = \"What is your name?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">뭐예요?</b> = \"what is it?\" — with 이름이 it asks for the name.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Answer: <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 …예요</span> or <span class=\"pt-ko\">제 이름은 …이에요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-3] Listening — 저는 가수예요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the sentence you hear.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 가수예요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u1q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>저는 친구예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not what you heard</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>저는 가수예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ you heard 가수 + 예요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>저는 팬이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ wrong word & ending</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>이름이 뭐예요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ a question, not heard</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u1q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The voice says <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 가수예요</span> — \"I am a singer.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">가수</b> has no 받침 so it is <b class=\"hl\">예요</b>, and <b class=\"hl\">저는</b> = \"as for me.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for the noun first, then catch the ending <span class=\"pt-ko\">-예요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-4] Reading — 받침 — 저는 아란이에요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct ending: \"I am Aran.\" (아란 has a final consonant ㄴ)</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 아란(     ).</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u1q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>이어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not the correct form</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>예요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 아란 has a 받침 (ㄴ)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>이에요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 아란 ends with ㄴ → 이에요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>이 있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ \"have Aran\" is odd</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u1q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">아란</b> ends in the final consonant <b class=\"hl\">ㄴ</b> (받침), so it needs the bridging <b class=\"hl\">이에요</b>: 저는 아란이에요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">예요</b> is only after a vowel — 아란's ㄴ makes 예요 sound unnatural.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Consonant ending → <span class=\"pt-ko\">이에요</span>. That is the exact rule from GRAMMAR 1.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-5] Reading — Formal — 입니다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read the answer and choose its meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">네, 학생입니다.</span> <span class=\"gl\">(answering a formal question)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u1q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>Yes, I am a student.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 입니다 = formal \"is/am\"; 네 = yes</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>No, I am a singer.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 아니요 would mean \"no\"</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>Thank you very much.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 감사합니다</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>I am a fan.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 팬이에요, not 학생입니다</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u1q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">네</span> = \"yes,\" and <span class=\"pt-ko\">학생입니다</span> = \"am a student\" in the <b class=\"hl\">formal</b> style.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">입니다</b> is the formal cousin of 이에요/예요 — used in announcements and stage greetings like <span class=\"pt-ko\">글로시스입니다!</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Question form: <span class=\"pt-ko\">…입니까?</span> → answer <span class=\"pt-ko\">…입니다</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-6] Listening — 안녕</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what the word means.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('안녕!')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u1q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>Good night.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 잘 자요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>Thank you.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 감사합니다</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>Hi! / Bye! (informal)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 안녕 is the casual hello/goodbye</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>Nice to meet you.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 만나서 반가워요</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u1q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You hear <span class=\"pt-ko\">안녕</span> — the <b class=\"hl\">casual</b> hello/goodbye used between friends.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ For polite situations Koreans say <b class=\"hl\">안녕하세요!</b> instead; 안녕 alone is very informal.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Use 안녕하세요 with strangers &amp; elders; save 안녕 for close friends.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-7] Reading — Vocab — 노래</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read the sentence and choose the meaning of 노래.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">글로시스의 노래가 좋아요.</span> <span class=\"gl\">(글로시스의 ___ is good)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u1q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>dance<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 춤</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>name<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 이름</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>stage<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 무대</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>song<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 노래 = \"song\"</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u1q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">In <span class=\"pt-ko\">글로시스의 노래</span> = \"Glowsis's <b class=\"hl\">song</b>,\" so 노래 means <b class=\"hl\">song</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ A singer performs <b class=\"hl\">노래</b> (song); the <b class=\"hl\">무대</b> (stage) is where they sing it.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 노래 = song — to say “to sing,” use <span class=\"pt-ko\">노래를 해요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-8] Listening — 저는 팬이에요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the sentence you hear.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 팬이에요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u1q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>저는 가수예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not what you heard</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>저는 팬이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 팬 ends with ㄴ → 이에요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>저는 팬예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ wrong ending (팬 has 받침)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>이름이 뭐예요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ a question, not heard</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u1q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The voice says <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 팬이에요</span> — \"I am a fan.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">팬</b> ends in the consonant <b class=\"hl\">ㄴ</b>, so it needs <b class=\"hl\">이에요</b>, not 예요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 팬 = \"fan\" — compare 팬<b class=\"hl\">이에요</b> vs 가수<b class=\"hl\">예요</b> to hear the 받침 rule.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-9] Reading — Vocab — 무대</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read the sentence and choose the meaning of 무대.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">글로시스는 무대에서 노래해요.</span> <span class=\"gl\">(Glowsis sings ___에서)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u1q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>fan<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 팬</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>friend<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 친구</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>stage<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 무대 = \"stage\"</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>name<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 이름</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u1q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">In <span class=\"pt-ko\">무대에서 노래해요</span> = \"sings <b class=\"hl\">on stage</b>,\" so 무대 means <b class=\"hl\">stage</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">노래</b> (song) happens <b class=\"hl\">on the 무대</b> (stage) — the two words live together.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 -에서 = \"at/in/on\" a place: <span class=\"pt-ko\">무대에서</span> = \"on stage.\"</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1-10] Listening — 감사합니다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what you hear.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('감사합니다!')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u1q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>Hello!<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 안녕하세요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>Thank you!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 감사합니다 = polite \"thank you\"</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>Goodbye!<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 안녕히 가세요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u1q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>Nice to meet you!<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 만나서 반가워요</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u1q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You hear <span class=\"pt-ko\">감사합니다!</span> — a warm, polite <b class=\"hl\">\"thank you!\"</b></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Idols thank fans with this at the end of every stage — right after <span class=\"pt-ko\">글로시스입니다!</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 감사합니다 is formal &amp; polite; in casual talk friends say <span class=\"pt-ko\">고마워</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"culture","html":"<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Idol Greeting Phrases, Like This!</h3>\n    <p>On music shows, idols greet like this: <b>\"안녕하세요, 글로시스입니다!\"</b> — when a member says their name, fans <b>scream</b>!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">🎵 Self-intro: \"안녕하세요! 저는 아란이에요. 글로시스의 리더예요.\" — Can you do it like Dahee?</div>\n  </div>\n\n<!-- ============================================================\n     UNIT 2 — SELF-INTRODUCTION\n     ============================================================ -->"}]},{"id":2,"sections":[{"cls":"unit-flag","html":"<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 2 · SELF-INTRODUCTION</div>\n  "},{"cls":"sec-title","html":"<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">2</div><div><h2>I'm a Singer</h2><div class=\"en\">저는 가수예요 — Self-introduction · N은/는</div></div></div>\n  "},{"cls":"story","html":"<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/story/u2.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 2/8</span>\n      <h3>채아의 자기소개 — \"저는 채아예요!\"</h3>\n      <p>분위기 메이커 <b>채아</b>는 데뷔 쇼케이스에서 <b>자기소개</b>를 가르쳐요. \"저는 ○○예요!\" — 소개할 때마다 팬들의 함성이 커져요. 💛</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Mood-maker <b>Chaea</b> teaches <b>self-introductions</b> at the debut showcase. \"저는 ○○예요!\" (I'm ○○!) — every introduction makes the fans cheer louder. 💛</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">💛 GLOW POINT 2/8 획득 — Self-introduction!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"},{"cls":"goals","html":"<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🗣️</span> Introduce yourself</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🔤</span> 은/는 topic particle</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🌍</span> Country & job vocabulary</div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"dialog","html":"<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 2 — Debut Interview</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">📺 Debut showcase</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">안녕하세요! 저는 채아예요. 글로시스의 보컬이에요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Hello! I'm Chaea. I'm Glowsis's vocalist.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 로이예요. 글로시스의 막내예요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I'm Roy. I'm Glowsis's maknae (youngest)!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 아란이에요. 한국 사람이에요. 글로시스의 리더예요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I'm Aran. I'm Korean. I'm Glowsis's leader!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 다희예요. 한국 사람이에요. 래퍼예요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I'm Dahee. I'm Korean. I'm a rapper.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">우리 팬들은 베트남 사람, 일본 사람, 캄보디아 사람이에요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Our fans are Vietnamese, Japanese, and Cambodian!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">은/는 — Topic particle</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Use it to introduce the topic of the sentence. After a final consonant use <b>은</b>, after a vowel use <b>는</b>. It feels like \"as for ~\"!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저<b>는</b> 채아예요.</span><span class=\"gl\">저 has no final consonant → 는</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">아란<b>은</b> 한국 사람이에요.</span><span class=\"gl\">아란 has final consonant ㄴ → 은</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이 노래<b>는</b> 좋아요.</span><span class=\"gl\">As for this song, I like it.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">N이에요/예요 — Talking about Jobs & Nationalities</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Self-introduction = name + nationality + job + role! Connect them all with <b>이에요/예요</b>.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 가수예요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I am a singer.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 학생이에요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I am a student.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 캄보디아 사람이에요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I am Cambodian.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n    "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">N도 — \"also / too\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Add <b>도</b> after a noun to say \"also, too\". It replaces 은/는 and 이/가. A favorite in TOPIK I!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 가수예요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I am also a singer.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">다희<b>도</b> 한국 사람이에요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Dahee is also Korean.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">노래<b>도</b> 좋아해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I like singing too.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"},{"cls":"teach","html":"<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"저는 가수예요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 가수예요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"As for me, I'm a singer.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Why does every K-POP self-introduction end in <b>예요 / 이에요</b> — and what is the <b>는</b> doing there?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      In English \"I am a singer\" is three words. Korean says the same idea but in the opposite order, and the verb\n      <b>\"to be\"</b> — <span class=\"pt-ko\">이다</span> — is glued onto the end as a polite little ending:\n      <b>저(는) 가수예요</b>. English: subject + verb + noun. Korean: topic <b>저는</b> + noun <b>가수</b> + polite <b>예요</b>.\n      There is no separate \"am / is\" word — the ending itself means <b>\"= is\"</b>.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">저<b>는</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">as for me <span class=\"t-sub\">(topic)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">저 = humble \"I\" (polite, used with fans). Add <b>는</b> to make it the topic. 저 ends in a vowel → 는.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">가수</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">singer <span class=\"t-sub\">(job)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">The noun comes <b>before</b> the verb, like all Korean sentences.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">예요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">= is <span class=\"t-sub\">(이다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">가수 ends in a vowel (ㅜ) → <b>예요</b>. After a consonant (학생·아란) we'd say <b>이에요</b>.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">은/는 = \"as for ~\"</b> — a topic marker that introduces WHAT you're talking about. <b>저는</b> = \"as for me…\".\n    Pick <b>는</b> after a vowel (저) and <b>은</b> after a consonant (아란<b>은</b>). It feels like saying\n    \"Me, I'm a singer\" — the topic first, the comment after.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Final consonant (받침) → 은 / 이에요</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">아란<b>은</b> 학생<b>이에요</b>.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">받침 = ㄴ·ㄱ·ㅁ… → \"Aran is a student.\"</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>No consonant (vowel) → 는 / 예요</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저<b>는</b> 가수<b>예요</b>.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">No 받침 = ㅓ·ㅜ·ㅏ… → \"I am a singer.\"</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> the SAME 받침 rule runs through both particles! <b>Consonant → 은 and 이에요</b>, <b>vowel → 는 and 예요</b>.\n    Add <b>도</b> (also) instead of 은/는 to say \"me too\": <span class=\"pt-ko\">저<b>도</b> 가수예요</span>. Fill in your country and job —\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 ○○ 사람이에요. ○○이에요</span> — and you can introduce yourself like an idol!\n  </div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"vocab-lab","html":"<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🌏</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">국적과 나라<small>Nationalities · 어디 사람이에요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_korean.webp\" alt=\"한국 사람\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('한국 사람')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">한국 사람</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hanguk saram</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Korean person</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_vietnam.webp\" alt=\"베트남 사람\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('베트남 사람')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">베트남 사람</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">betnam saram</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Vietnamese person</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_japan.webp\" alt=\"일본 사람\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('일본 사람')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">일본 사람</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ilbon saram</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Japanese person</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_cambodia.webp\" alt=\"캄보디아 사람\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('캄보디아 사람')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">캄보디아 사람</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">kambodia saram</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Cambodian person</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 한국 사람이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 한국 사람이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I am Korean.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('유나는 베트남 사람이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">유나는 베트남 사람이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Yuna is Vietnamese.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지훈은 일본 사람이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">지훈은 일본 사람이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Jihoon is Japanese.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('팬들은 캄보디아 사람이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">팬들은 캄보디아 사람이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The fans are Cambodian.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아란 씨도 한국 사람이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아란 씨도 한국 사람이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Aran is Korean too.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🤝 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 나라 + 사람 = nationality. 한국+사람=한국 사람, 베트남+사람=베트남 사람. To say a nationality you literally say \"<b>country + person</b>\".</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎤</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">아이돌 포지션<small>Idol roles · 그룹 안에서 하는 일</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">5</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_vocal.webp\" alt=\"보컬\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('보컬')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">보컬</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">bokeol</div><div class=\"vw-en\">vocalist</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_rapper.webp\" alt=\"래퍼\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('래퍼')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">래퍼</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">raepeo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">rapper</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_leader.webp\" alt=\"리더\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('리더')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">리더</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">rideo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">leader</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_dancer.webp\" alt=\"댄서\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('댄서')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">댄서</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">daenseo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">dancer</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_maknae.webp\" alt=\"막내\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('막내')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">막내</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">mangnae</div><div class=\"vw-en\">youngest member</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 보컬이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 보컬이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'm the vocalist.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('다희는 래퍼예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">다희는 래퍼예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Dahee is the rapper.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아란은 리더예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아란은 리더예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Aran is the leader.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('유나는 메인 댄서예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">유나는 메인 댄서예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Yuna is the main dancer.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('로이는 글로시스의 막내예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">로이는 글로시스의 막내예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Roy is Glowsis's youngest (maknae).</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🎤 <b>한 그룹의 역할:</b> 글로시스 = 리더(아란) + 보컬(채아·서연) + 래퍼(다희·지훈) + 댄서(유나) + 막내(로이). Each member says \"제 역할은 …이에요/예요\".</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">💼</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">직업<small>Jobs · 무엇을 해요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">5</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_student.webp\" alt=\"학생\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('학생')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">학생</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">haksaeng</div><div class=\"vw-en\">student</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_worker.webp\" alt=\"회사원\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('회사원')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">회사원</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hoesawon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">office worker</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_teacher.webp\" alt=\"선생님\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('선생님')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">선생님</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">seonsaengnim</div><div class=\"vw-en\">teacher</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_doctor.webp\" alt=\"의사\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('의사')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">의사</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">uisa</div><div class=\"vw-en\">doctor</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_police.webp\" alt=\"경찰\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('경찰')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">경찰</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gyeongchal</div><div class=\"vw-en\">police officer</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 학생이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 학생이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I am a student.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('형은 회사원이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">형은 회사원이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">My older brother is an office worker.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어머니는 선생님이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">어머니는 선생님이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">My mother is a teacher.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아버지는 의사예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아버지는 의사예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">My father is a doctor.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 경찰이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 경찰이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I am a police officer.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">💼 <b>직업 + 이에요/예요:</b> Say your job with <b>이에요</b> (받침: 학생·선생님·회사원·경찰) or <b>예요</b> (vowel: 의사). Almost every job can go here!</div></div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2-1] Reading — 아란은 (은/는)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct topic particle.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">아란 씨(　) 한국 사람이에요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u2q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 은<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 아란 ends in the consonant ㄴ → 은</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 는<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 는 needs a word that ends in a vowel</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 을<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 을 is the object particle</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 가<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 가 is the subject particle</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u2q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The noun <span class=\"pt-ko\">아란</span> ends in the final consonant <b class=\"hl\">ㄴ</b> (받침), so the topic particle must be <b class=\"hl\">은</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">아란은</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">는</b> is only used after a vowel (저는); <b class=\"hl\">을</b> marks the object and <b class=\"hl\">가</b> marks the subject, not the topic.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: 받침(consonant) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">은</span>; vowel → <span class=\"pt-ko\">는</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2-2] Reading — 가수예요 (이에요/예요)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence is correct?</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">다음 중 맞는 문장을 고르세요. (Choose the correct sentence.)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u2q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>저는 가수예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 가수 ends in a vowel → 예요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>저는 가수이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 이에요 is for words with 받침</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>저는 학생예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 학생 has 받침 → 학생이에요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>아란은 한국 사람예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 사람 has 받침 → 사람이에요</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u2q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Polite \"to be\" = <b class=\"hl\">예요</b> after a vowel, <b class=\"hl\">이에요</b> after a consonant. <span class=\"pt-ko\">가수</span> ends in the vowel ㅜ, so <span class=\"pt-ko\">가수예요</span> is correct.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">가수이에요</b> is wrong (가수 has no 받침), and <b class=\"hl\">학생예요 / 사람예요</b> are wrong because 학생·사람 DO have 받침 and need 이에요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Same 받침 rule as 은/는 — consonant → <span class=\"pt-ko\">이에요</span>, vowel → <span class=\"pt-ko\">예요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2-3] Reading — 저도 (도 = also)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the particle that means \"also / too\".</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">저는 가수예요. 제 친구(　) 가수예요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u2q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 도<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 도 = \"also\": my friend is a singer TOO</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 는<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 는 just marks the topic</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 은<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 은 also just marks the topic</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 가<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 가 marks the subject</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u2q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You want to say my friend is a singer <b class=\"hl\">too</b>. The particle <span class=\"pt-ko\">도</span> replaces 은/는 and means \"also / too\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">는/은</b> only mark the topic and <b class=\"hl\">가</b> marks the subject — none add \"also\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">저도 가수예요</span> = \"I'm a singer too\" — 도 swaps straight into the 은/는 slot.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2-4] Reading — 막내 (roles)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct word.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">저는 글로시스에서 가장 어려요. 저는 (　)이에요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u2q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 막내<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 막내 = the youngest member</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 리더<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 리더 = leader</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 보컬<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 보컬 = vocalist</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 댄서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 댄서 = dancer</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u2q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">\"가장 어려요\" = I'm the <b class=\"hl\">youngest</b>. The youngest member of a group is the <span class=\"pt-ko\">막내</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">리더</b> leads the group, <b class=\"hl\">보컬</b> sings, <b class=\"hl\">댄서</b> dances — none mean \"youngest\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 In K-POP the maknae is a beloved role — 로이 is Glowsis's maknae!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2-5] Reading — 베트남 사람 (nationality)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read the introduction and answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"안녕하세요! 저는 유나예요. 저는 베트남 사람이에요.\" — 유나 씨는 어느 나라 사람이에요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u2q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>베트남 사람<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ She says 베트남 사람이에요 = Vietnamese</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>한국 사람<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Korean is not what she says</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>일본 사람<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ She is not Japanese</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>캄보디아 사람<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ She is not Cambodian</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u2q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The passage says <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 베트남 사람이에요</span> = \"I am <b class=\"hl\">Vietnamese</b>.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others name nationalities (한국/일본/캄보디아) not in the text.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Nationality = country + 사람: <span class=\"pt-ko\">베트남 + 사람</span> = Vietnamese person.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2-6] Reading — 어머니도 (도 comprehension)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"아버지는 의사예요. 어머니도 의사예요.\" — 어머니는 무슨 일을 해요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u2q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>의사예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ Mother is a doctor too (도).</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>경찰이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ No police officer here</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>학생이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not a student</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>회사원이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not an office worker</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u2q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Father is a doctor <b class=\"hl\">and</b> mother is a doctor <b class=\"hl\">too</b> (<span class=\"pt-ko\">어머니도 의사예요</span>), so she is a <b class=\"hl\">의사</b> (doctor).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 경찰/학생/회사원 are jobs not mentioned — the <span class=\"pt-ko\">도</span> says she shares the father's job.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Watch for <span class=\"pt-ko\">도</span>: it means the next person shares the same fact.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2-7] Listening — 회사원이에요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what the person's job is.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 회사원이에요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What does the speaker do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u2q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>회사원<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 회사원이에요 = office worker</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>의사<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not a doctor</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>경찰<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not a police officer</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>선생님<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not a teacher</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u2q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 회사원이에요</span> = \"I am an <b class=\"hl\">office worker</b>.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The other jobs (의사/경찰/선생님) were not said.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 회사원 has 받침 ㄴ → it takes <span class=\"pt-ko\">이에요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2-8] Listening — 로이는 막내</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose who/what is being described.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 로이예요. 글로시스의 막내예요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What role does Roy have in Glowsis?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u2q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>리더<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Leader is a different role</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>막내<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 막내예요 = youngest member</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>래퍼<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not a rapper here</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>보컬<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not a vocalist here</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u2q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 로이예요. 글로시스의 막내예요</span> — Roy is the <b class=\"hl\">막내</b> (youngest member).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 리더/래퍼/보컬 are other roles; the key word you hear is <b class=\"hl\">막내</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 막내 ends in a vowel (ㅐ) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">막내예요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2-9] Listening — 서연 씨도 보컬</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose Seoyeon's role.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('채아는 보컬이에요. 서연 씨도 보컬이에요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">서연 씨는 뭐예요? (What is Seoyeon?)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u2q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>보컬<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 도 = Seoyeon is a vocalist TOO</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>댄서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not a dancer</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>리더<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not the leader</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>래퍼<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not a rapper</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u2q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">채아는 보컬이에요. 서연 씨도 보컬이에요</span> — the <span class=\"pt-ko\">도</span> means Seoyeon is a vocalist <b class=\"hl\">too</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 댄서/리더/래퍼 are other roles not mentioned for Seoyeon.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 In listening, <b class=\"hl\">도</b> before the repeated word tells you two people share the same job.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2-10] Listening — 일본 사람 & 학생</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the best summary.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 일본 사람이에요. 저는 학생이에요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Who is the speaker?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u2q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>일본 사람 & 학생<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ Japanese and a student — both heard</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>한국 사람 & 학생<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ He is not Korean</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>일본 사람 & 선생님<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not a teacher</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u2q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>베트남 사람 & 회사원<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Neither was said</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u2q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker says <span class=\"pt-ko\">일본 사람이에요</span> (Japanese) and <span class=\"pt-ko\">학생이에요</span> (student) — best summary is <b class=\"hl\">Japanese + student</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others mix nationalities/jobs not said (한국/베트남, 선생님/회사원).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Connect two self-intro facts — nationality (나라+사람) and job — both end in <span class=\"pt-ko\">이에요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"culture","html":"<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Self-Introduction Challenge!</h3>\n    <p>Idols make a <b>self-introduction phrase</b> when they debut. Shall we make one too?</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ \"안녕하세요! 저는 ○○예요. ○○ 사람이에요. ○○이에요!\" — Fill in your name, country, and job!</div>\n  </div>\n\n<!-- ============================================================\n     UNIT 3 — THINGS\n     ============================================================ -->"}]},{"id":3,"sections":[{"cls":"unit-flag","html":"<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 3 · THINGS</div>\n  "},{"cls":"sec-title","html":"<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">3</div><div><h2>What is This?</h2><div class=\"en\">이거 뭐예요? — Things · 이/그/저</div></div></div>\n  "},{"cls":"story","html":"<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/story/u3.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 3/8</span>\n      <h3>다희의 보물 상자 — \"이거 뭐예요?\"</h3>\n      <p>메인댄서 <b>다희</b>는 신기한 물건들을 발견해요 — 응원봉, 포토카드, 앨범! 물건의 이름을 알면 팬들에게 자랑할 수 있어요. \"이거 뭐예요?\"라고 물어보세요! ⭐</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Main dancer <b>Dahee</b> discovers amazing objects — light sticks, photocards, albums! If you know the names of things, you can show them off to fans. Ask \"이거 뭐예요?\" (What is this?)! ⭐</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">🎁 GLOW POINT 3/8 획득 — Things!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"},{"cls":"goals","html":"<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">👉</span> 이/그/저 demonstratives</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🎒</span> Object vocabulary</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">✅</span> 있어요/없어요</div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"dialog","html":"<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 3 — Making Merch</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎁 Merch meeting</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">이거 뭐예요?</div><div class=\"gl\">What is this?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">이거는 응원봉이에요. 팬들이 콘서트에서 써요.</div><div class=\"gl\">This is a light stick. Fans use it at concerts.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">그거는 뭐예요?</div><div class=\"gl\">What is that?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">그거는 앨범이에요. 사진하고 포토카드가 있어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">That is an album. It has photos and photocards.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">포토카드 있어요? 저거 주세요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Is there a photocard? Give me that one!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">이/그/저 — This / That / That over there</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">이 = something near me, 그 = something near you, 저 = something far from both.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이거는 응원봉이에요.</span><span class=\"gl\">This (near me) is a light stick.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">그거는 앨범이에요.</span><span class=\"gl\">That (near you) is an album.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저거 주세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Please give me that one (over there).</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">N이/가 있어요 · 없어요 — There is / There isn't</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Essential for TOPIK I! <b>있어요</b> = 있다 (to exist / to have), <b>없어요</b> = 없다 (to not exist).</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">포토카드가 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">There is a photocard.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">시간이 없어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I don't have time.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">연습실에 거울이 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">There is a mirror in the practice room.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n    "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">N 주세요 — \"Please give me N\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Ask for something politely. Essential for shopping, ordering, and merch booths!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">포토카드 주세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Please give me the photocard.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">물 주세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Please give me water.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저거 주세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Please give me that one (over there).</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n\n<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"이거 뭐예요?\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">이거 뭐예요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"What is this?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Why do Koreans say it this way — and how is it different from the textbook form?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      Written out fully, it should be <b>\"이거<b class=\"hl\">는</b> 뭐예요?\"</b>. But in everyday spoken Korean,<br>\n      when you're pointing at something right in front of you, native speakers <b>drop the topic particle 은/는</b> and simply ask <b>\"이거 뭐예요?\"</b> — much more natural.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">이거</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">this <span class=\"t-sub\">(near me)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Spoken, shortened form of 이것.<br><b>이+것 → 이거</b> (것 → 거)</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-qcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">뭐</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">what <span class=\"t-sub\">(question word)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Short form of 무엇.<br>뭐예요? = \"뭐 + 예요?\"</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">예요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">= is <span class=\"t-sub\">(이다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">뭐<b>예요</b> = 무엇<b>이에요</b>.<br>After a vowel (ㅓ in 뭐) we use 예요.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">\"이거 뭐예요?\"</b> = 이거<b>(는)</b> 뭐예요? → When the thing you're asking about is <b>right in front of you</b>, you skip 은/는. You're already pointing at it, so the listener knows *what* it is — you only want to know <b>what it's called</b>.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Textbook (full form)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">이거<b>는</b> 뭐예요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">Grammar-perfect, when contrasting</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Real speech (natural)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">이거 뭐예요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">Everyday, pointing at something ✨</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> In \"What is this?\" → what = <b>뭐</b>, is = <b>예요</b> (이다), this = <b>이거</b>. But Korean puts the <b>topic first</b> and the <b>question last</b>: 이거 (이건 뭐냐?) → 뭐예요. So you get \"이거 뭐예요?\";\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎁</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">팬 굿즈<small>Fan Goods · 콘서트에서 쓰는 물건</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/lightstick.webp\"\" alt=\"응원봉\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('응원봉')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">응원봉</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eungwonbong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">light stick</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/album.webp\"\" alt=\"앨범\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('앨범')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">앨범</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">aelbeom</div><div class=\"vw-en\">album</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/photocard.webp\"\" alt=\"포토카드\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('포토카드')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">포토카드</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">potokadeu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">photocard</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/tshirt.webp\"\" alt=\"티셔츠\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('티셔츠')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">티셔츠</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">tisyeocheu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">T-shirt</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('응원봉을 들어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">응원봉을 들어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Hold up the light stick.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('콘서트에서 응원봉을 들어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">콘서트에서 응원봉을 들어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We wave light sticks at the concert.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('앨범을 사요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">앨범을 사요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I buy an album.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('앨범에 좋은 노래가 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">앨범에 좋은 노래가 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The album has great songs.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('포토카드를 모아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">포토카드를 모아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I collect photocards.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('글로시스 티셔츠를 입어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">글로시스 티셔츠를 입어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I wear the Glowsis T-shirt.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🤝 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> 응원봉은 <b>들다</b>, 앨범은 <b>사다·듣다</b>, 포토카드는 <b>모으다</b>와 잘 어울려요. 팬 굿즈는 전부 <b>콘서트</b>에서 나와요!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎧</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">폰 & 음악<small>Phone · Music · 사진 찍기</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/phone.webp\"\" alt=\"휴대폰\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('휴대폰')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">휴대폰</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hyudaepon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cell phone</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/earphones.webp\"\" alt=\"이어폰\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이어폰')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">이어폰</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ieopon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">earphones</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/photo.webp\"\" alt=\"사진\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('사진')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">사진</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sajin</div><div class=\"vw-en\">photo</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('휴대폰으로 사진을 찍어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">휴대폰으로 사진을 찍어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I take photos with my phone.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('휴대폰이 없어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">휴대폰이 없어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I don't have a phone.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이어폰으로 음악을 들어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이어폰으로 음악을 들어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I listen to music with earphones.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('사진을 찍어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">사진을 찍어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I take a picture.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🖼️ <b>같은 짝:</b> 포토카드(굿즈)는 '아이돌 사진'이에요. <b>사진 ↔ 포토카드</b> — 둘 다 '찍고 / 모아요'. 이어폰으로는 <b>노래</b>를 들어요.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎒</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">매일 챙기는 것<small>Daily carry · 있어요/없어요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/bag.webp\"\" alt=\"가방\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가방')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">가방</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gabang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">bag</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/umbrella.webp\"\" alt=\"우산\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('우산')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">우산</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">usan</div><div class=\"vw-en\">umbrella</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/key.webp\"\" alt=\"열쇠\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('열쇠')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">열쇠</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeolsoe</div><div class=\"vw-en\">key</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/watch.webp\"\" alt=\"시계\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시계')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">시계</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sigye</div><div class=\"vw-en\">watch, clock</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가방에 책이 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">가방에 책이 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">There's a book in the bag.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가방에 열쇠가 있어요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">가방에 열쇠가 있어요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Is there a key in the bag?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('비가 와요. 우산을 써요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">비가 와요. 우산을 써요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It's raining. Use an umbrella.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('열쇠가 없어요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">열쇠가 없어요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I don't have the key!</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시계를 봐요. 몇 시예요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">시계를 봐요. 몇 시예요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Look at the watch. What time is it?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">⚖️ <b>반대 짝:</b> 있어요 ↔ 없어요 (GRAMMAR 2). 가방 <b>에</b> 열쇠가 있어요 / 없어요 — 다 '가지고 있냐 없냐'로 말해요.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">📖</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">공부 & 연습<small>Study & practice room</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/book.webp\"\" alt=\"책\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('책')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">책</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chaek</div><div class=\"vw-en\">book</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/mirror.webp\"\" alt=\"거울\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('거울')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">거울</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">geoul</div><div class=\"vw-en\">mirror</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('책을 읽어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">책을 읽어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I read a book.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('연습실에서 거울을 봐요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">연습실에서 거울을 봐요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I look in the mirror in the practice room.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('거울을 보며 춤을 춰요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">거울을 보며 춤을 춰요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I dance while watching the mirror.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🔤 <b>둘 다 보는 물건:</b> 책은 <b>읽다</b>, 거울은 <b>보다</b>. 글로시스는 연습실 거울로 춤을 연습해요!</div></div></div></div>\n\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-1] Reading — Picture: 있어요 vs 없어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Look at the picture and choose the correct sentence.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">[그림: 기타 1개] Read and choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u3q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>기타가 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ There IS a guitar — the picture has one.</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>기타가 없어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>기타가 좋아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>기타가 커요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u3q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">사진에 기타가 <b class=\"hl\">1개 보이므로</b> “있다” = <b class=\"hl\">있어요</b>가 정답이에요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">없어요</b>=없다, <b class=\"hl\">좋아요</b>=좋다, <b class=\"hl\">커요</b>=크다 — 전부 존재와 달라요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">이/가 있어요</span> = “~이 있다”. 물건이 보이면 있어요!</div></div></div>\n</div>\n\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-2] Listening — 가방에 책이 있어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what you hear.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('가방에 책이 있어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u3q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>가방에 책이 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 책이 있어요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>가방에 책이 없어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>가방이 책이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>책이 가방이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u3q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">음성은 <span class=\"pt-ko\">가방에 책이 있어요</span> — “책이 있다”.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">없어요</b>는 뜻이 반대, <b class=\"hl\">이에요</b>는 “=이다”라 어색해요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 듣기는 끝말 <b class=\"hl\">있어요/없어요/이에요</b>를 먼저 잡으세요!</div></div></div>\n</div>\n\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-3] Listening — At the Merch Booth (주세요)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what the fan says at the booth.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('포토카드 주세요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u3q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>포토카드 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ Please give me the photocard.</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>포토카드 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>포토카드 없어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>포토카드 좋아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u3q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">가게에서 물건을 살 땐 <span class=\"pt-ko\">주세요</span>(주다=give)로 요청해요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 있어요/없어요=상태, 좋아요=느낌 — <b class=\"hl\">무엇을 달라</b>는 요청이 아니에요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 쇼핑·굿즈 부스는 무조건 <b class=\"hl\">… 주세요</b>!</div></div></div>\n</div>\n\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-4] Reading — 이거/그거/저거 고르기</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">아란이 옆에서 사진을 들고 “이거는 뭐예요?”라고 물어요. 사진이 아란에게 가까이 있어요.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">사진이 <b>말하는 사람에게 가까울 때</b> 뭐라고 하나요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u3q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>이거는 뭐예요?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ near me → 이</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>그거는 뭐예요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>저거는 뭐예요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>뭐는 이거예요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u3q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">사진이 <b class=\"hl\">나에게 가까우면</b> <span class=\"pt-ko\">이거</span>!</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">그거</b>=상대 가까이, <b class=\"hl\">저거</b>=둘 다에게 먼 곳.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 거리: 내 코앞=<b class=\"hl\">이</b>, 네 옆=<b class=\"hl\">그</b>, 저 멀리=<b class=\"hl\">저</b>!</div></div></div>\n</div>\n\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-5] Reading — 물건 어휘 (거울 있어요)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">다음 문장을 읽고 뜻을 고르세요.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">연습실에 거울이 있어요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u3q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>There is no mirror.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>The mirror is an idol.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>There is a mirror in the practice room.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 거울이 있어요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>I like the mirror.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u3q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">연습실에</span>=in the practice room, <span class=\"pt-ko\">거울이 있어요</span>=there is a mirror.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">있어요</b>=있다, <b class=\"hl\">이에요</b>=이다, <b class=\"hl\">좋아요</b>=좋다 — 전부 달라요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">장소에 ~이/가 있어요</b> = “장소에 ~이 있다”.</div></div></div>\n</div>\n\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-6] Listening — 저거 주세요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 판매대 멀리 있는 앨범을 가리키며 말해요.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저거 주세요.')\">🔊 Listen (저거 주세요)</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u3q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>저거 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ far → 저 + 주세요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>이거 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>그거 있어요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>저거 좋아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u3q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">멀리 있는 걸 원하면 <span class=\"pt-ko\">저거 주세요</span>! (<b class=\"hl\">저</b>=far)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 멀리 있으면 반드시 <b class=\"hl\">저</b>. 이=내 옆, 그=네 옆.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 부스에서 저 멀리 앨범 가리킬 때 딱!</div></div></div>\n</div>\n\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-7] Reading — 부정문 (없어요)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">다음을 읽고 뜻을 고르세요.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">시간이 없어요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u3q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>There is no time.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 없어요 = is not</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>There is time.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>Time is fun.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>I have a watch.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u3q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">없어요</span> = “없다”. → “시간이 없다” = There is no time.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">있어요 ↔ 없어요</b>는 반대 짝. 없이 들리면 반대로!</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 GRAMMAR 2가 바로 이 있어요/없어요예요.</div></div></div>\n</div>\n\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-8] Reading — 저거 (picture)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">그림을 보고 맞는 문장을 고르세요.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">[그림: 저 멀리 축구공] — 공이 우리에게서 멀어요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u3q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>이거는 공이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>그거는 공이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>저거는 공이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ far → 저</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>공은 없어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u3q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">공이 <b class=\"hl\">둘 다에게 먼 곳</b>이니 <span class=\"pt-ko\">저거</span>가 맞아요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 보이는데 “없다”는 <b class=\"hl\">없어요</b>는 바로 틀려요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 공은 받침 ㄱ... 아니 “공”은 받침 ㅇ! 그래서 <b class=\"hl\">공이에요</b>가 맞아요.</div></div></div>\n</div>\n\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-9] Listening — 있어요? 질문</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 가게에서 물어봐요. 알맞은 답을 고르세요.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('포토카드 있어요?')\">🔊 Listen (포토카드 있어요?)</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u3q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>네, 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ yes, there is</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>네, 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>아니요, 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>포토카드가 좋아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u3q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">“있어요?”는 “있나요?” — 답은 <span class=\"pt-ko\">네, 있어요</span> / <b class=\"hl\">아니요, 없어요</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">네+없어요</b>, <b class=\"hl\">아니요+있어요</b>는 모순이라 틀려요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 부정 질문이 아니면 네=있어요, 아니요=없어요!</div></div></div>\n</div>\n\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3-10] Reading — 주세요 vs 있어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">아란이 응원봉을 사려고 해요. 가장 자연스러운 말을 고르세요.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Glowsis 굿즈 판매대 앞에서 아란이:</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u3q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>응원봉 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ polite request to buy</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>응원봉이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>응원봉이 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u3q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>응원봉이 좋아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u3q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">물건을 <b class=\"hl\">사고 싶을 때</b>는 “… 주세요”로 요청해요. → <span class=\"pt-ko\">응원봉 주세요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 이에요(정체), 있어요(존재), 좋아요(감정)는 <b class=\"hl\">요청</b>이 아니에요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 구매 의도=<b class=\"hl\">주세요</b>, 존재 확인=<b class=\"hl\">있어요?</b>!</div></div></div>\n</div>\n\n"},{"cls":"culture","html":"<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Merch Vocabulary Dictionary</h3>\n    <p>Every idol group has a different light stick color and shape! Fans collect <b>photocards</b> and buy <b>albums</b>.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">🛍️ When shopping: \"이거 얼마예요?\" (How much is this?) — you'll learn it in Unit 9!</div>\n  </div>\n\n<!-- ============================================================\n     UNIT 4 — NUMBERS & DATES\n     ============================================================ -->"}]},{"id":4,"sections":[{"cls":"unit-flag","html":"<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 4 · NUMBERS & DATES</div>\n  "},{"cls":"sec-title","html":"<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">4</div><div><h2>Debut is in May</h2><div class=\"en\">데뷔는 5월이에요 — Numbers · Dates · Days</div></div></div>\n  "},{"cls":"story","html":"<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/story/u4.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 4/8</span>\n      <h3>로이의 데뷔 캘린더 — \"5월 20일!\"</h3>\n      <p>막내 <b>로이</b>는 데뷔 날짜를 기다리고 있어요. 데뷔 캘린더를 읽으려면 <b>숫자와 날짜, 요일</b>이 필요해요! \"언제예요?\" — 날짜를 말할수록 데뷔가 가까워져요. 🐰</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">The youngest, <b>Roy</b>, is waiting for debut day. To read the debut calendar you need <b>numbers, dates, and days of the week</b>! \"언제예요?\" (When is it?) — the more dates you say, the closer debut gets. 🐰</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">📆 GLOW POINT 4/8 획득 — Numbers & Dates!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"},{"cls":"goals","html":"<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🔢</span> Native Korean numbers (하나~열)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">📅</span> Sino-Korean numbers & dates</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🗓️</span> Days of the week</div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"dialog","html":"<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 4 — Setting the Debut Date</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">📆 Manager meeting</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">데뷔는 5월 17일이에요. 무슨 요일이에요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Debut is May 17th. What day of the week is it?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">일요일이에요!</div><div class=\"gl\">It's Sunday!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">음악방송은 금요일이에요. 데뷔 무대는 5월 20일이에요!</div><div class=\"gl\">The music show is on Friday. The debut stage is May 20th!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 5월 20일, 금요일이에요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Great! May 20th, Friday!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">Numbers — Native vs Sino-Korean</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">하나, 둘, 셋 = <b>native Korean</b> (for counting: noun + 개). 일, 이, 삼 = <b>Sino-Korean</b> (dates, time, prices).</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">하나, 둘, 셋, 넷, 다섯, 여섯, 일곱, 여덟, 아홉, 열</span><span class=\"gl\">1-10 native Korean</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">일, 이, 삼, 사, 오, 육, 칠, 팔, 구, 십</span><span class=\"gl\">1-10 Sino-Korean</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">사과 세 개 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">There are three apples. (개 = counter)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">Dates and Days of the Week</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Dates use Sino-Korean: <b>N월 N일</b>. Days: 월·화·수·목·금·토·일 + 요일.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">5월 17일</span><span class=\"gl\">May 17th (오월 십칠일)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">월요일, 화요일, 수요일, 목요일, 금요일, 토요일, 일요일</span><span class=\"gl\">Mon–Sun</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">오늘은 금요일이에요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Today is Friday.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">생일이 언제예요? — 5월 17일이에요.</span><span class=\"gl\">When is your birthday? — May 17th. (TOPIK 필수!)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n    "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">시간 — N시 N분 (telling time)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Time uses Sino-Korean numbers: <b>N시 N분</b>. \"What time is it?\" = <b>몇 시예요?</b></div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지금 몇 시예요? — 5시예요.</span><span class=\"gl\">What time is it now? — It's 5 o'clock.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">9시 30분이에요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It's 9:30.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">데뷔 무대는 6시에 시작해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">The debut stage starts at 6 o'clock.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"},{"cls":"teach","html":"<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Why are there TWO sets of numbers? (하나 vs 일)</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">두 시예요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"It's two o'clock.\" — but why 두, not 이 or 둘?</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Korean has two number systems — and telling time uses BOTH at once. Here's the \"why\".</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      There are <b>native Korean numbers</b> (<span class=\"pt-ko\">하나, 둘, 셋, 넷…</span>) used for <b>counting objects</b> and the <b>hour on a clock</b>, and <b>Sino-Korean numbers</b> (<span class=\"pt-ko\">일, 이, 삼, 사…</span>) used for <b>minutes, months, dates, and prices</b>. So a clock mixes them: the <b>hour is native</b>, the <b>minutes are Sino</b>.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">두</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">two <span class=\"t-sub\">(native, hour)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">둘 → <b>두</b> before 시.<br>Right before the word \"hour\",<br>하나·둘·셋·넷 shorten to 한·두·세·네.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">시</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">o'clock <span class=\"t-sub\">(hour counter)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Native number + 시 = the hour.<br>다섯 시 = 5 o'clock, 열두 시 = noon.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">예요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">= is <span class=\"t-sub\">(이다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Polite \"is\" ending.<br>두 시<b>예요</b> = It's two o'clock.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">\"두 시 십오 분\"</b> = <b>native hour</b> (<span class=\"t-ko\">두 시</span>) + <b>Sino minutes</b> (<span class=\"t-ko\">십오 분</span>). One sentence, two systems! Dates work the same way — they are <b>all Sino</b>: <span class=\"t-ko\">이월 십사일</span> (Feb 14).\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>What beginners guess</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">이 시 십사 분</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">Sino everywhere — sounds stiff &amp; wrong</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>What Koreans say</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">두 시 십사 분</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">Native hour + Sino minutes ✨</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> On a clock, <b>the hour is a \"native\" friend</b> (한 두 세 네) but <b>every minute is \"Sino\"</b> (일 이 삼…). And a full date is 100% Sino, top to bottom: <b>2월 14일 → 이월 십사일</b>. When someone asks <b>몇 시예요?</b> you answer with the native hour + Sino minutes.\n  </div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"vocab-lab","html":"<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🗓️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">요일<small>Days of the week · 월요일~일요일</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">7</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_mon.webp\" alt=\"월요일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('월요일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">월요일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">woryoil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Monday</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_tue.webp\" alt=\"화요일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('화요일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">화요일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hwayoil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Tuesday</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_wed.webp\" alt=\"수요일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('수요일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">수요일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">suyoil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Wednesday</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_thu.webp\" alt=\"목요일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('목요일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">목요일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">mogyoil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Thursday</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_fri.webp\" alt=\"금요일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('금요일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">금요일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">geumyoil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Friday</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_sat.webp\" alt=\"토요일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('토요일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">토요일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">toyoil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Saturday</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_sun.webp\" alt=\"일요일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('일요일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">일요일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">iryoil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Sunday</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘은 금요일이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오늘은 금요일이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Today is Friday.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('월요일에 학교에 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">월요일에 학교에 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go to school on Monday.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('토요일에 콘서트에 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">토요일에 콘서트에 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go to the concert on Saturday.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('데뷔 무대는 금요일이에요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">데뷔 무대는 금요일이에요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The debut stage is on Friday!</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('일요일은 쉬어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">일요일은 쉬어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I rest on Sunday.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🤝 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> 모든 요일은 <b>월화수목금토일 + 요일</b>. 무슨 요일이에요? = \"What day is it?\" — 요일 뒤에 <b>이에요/이 아니에요</b>가 와요. 데뷔 날은 바로 <b>금요일</b>!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">⏰</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">시간대<small>Time of day · 아침/오늘/밤</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_morning.webp\" alt=\"아침\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아침')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">아침</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">achim</div><div class=\"vw-en\">morning</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_today.webp\" alt=\"오늘\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">오늘</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">oneul</div><div class=\"vw-en\">today</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_night.webp\" alt=\"밤\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('밤')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">밤</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">bam</div><div class=\"vw-en\">night</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아침 일곱 시에 일어나요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아침 일곱 시에 일어나요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I wake up at 7 in the morning.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('밤 열 시에 잠을 자요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">밤 열 시에 잠을 자요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I sleep at 10 at night.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘은 아주 바빠요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오늘은 아주 바빠요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Today is very busy.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아침에는 연습하고 밤에는 쉬어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아침에는 연습하고 밤에는 쉬어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Morning = practice, night = rest.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🌗 <b>반대 짝:</b> <b>아침 ↔ 밤</b> (morning vs night). <b>오늘</b> = today. \"시간\"은 언제인지 말할 때 꼭 필요한 말이에요 — 아침·밤을 배우면 하루 일과를 말할 수 있어요!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎂</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">생일 · 시간 묻기<small>Asking birthday & time · 생일/언제/몇 시</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_birthday.webp\" alt=\"생일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('생일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">생일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">saengil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">birthday</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_when.webp\" alt=\"언제\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('언제')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">언제</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eonje</div><div class=\"vw-en\">when</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u4_time.webp\" alt=\"몇 시\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('몇 시')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">몇 시</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">myeot si</div><div class=\"vw-en\">what time</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('생일이 언제예요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">생일이 언제예요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">When is your birthday?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('제 생일은 오월 십칠일이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">제 생일은 오월 십칠일이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">My birthday is May 17th.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지금 몇 시예요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">지금 몇 시예요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">What time is it now?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('여덟 시예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">여덟 시예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It's eight o'clock.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('생일 축하해요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">생일 축하해요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Happy birthday!</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">❓ <b>묻는 법:</b> <b>언제</b> = \"when\" (생일이 <b>언제</b>예요?). <b>몇 시</b> = \"what time\" (지금 <b>몇 시</b>예요?). 날짜는 전부 Sino로 읽어요 — <b>이월 십사일</b> = Feb 14!</div></div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-1] Reading — Counting: native numbers</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Read the sentence and choose what it means.</div><div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">사과가 두 개 있어요.</span></div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u4q1\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>사과가 셋 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>There are two apples.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 두 개 = two (native) + 개 counter</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>There are three apples.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>There is no apple.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u4q1\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">두</b> = native Korean “two” and <b class=\"hl\">개</b> = the counter for objects. <span class=\"pt-ko\">두 개</span> = “two (of them).” So “There are two apples.”</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">셋</b> = three (native), not two. <b class=\"hl\">없어요</b> = “there isn’t.”</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Counting objects = <b class=\"hl\">native numbers + 개</b> (하나 둘 셋 넷…).</div></div></div>\n</div>\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-2] Reading — Find the day of the week</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Read the calendar note and choose the correct day.</div><div class=\"p-passage\">데뷔 무대 — 5월 20일 (Fri)</div><div class=\"p-q\">What day of the week is the debut stage?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u4q2\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>수요일<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>목요일<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>금요일<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 金 = 금, so Fri = 금요일</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>토요일<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u4q2\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The note says <span class=\"pt-ko\">금요일</span> (Friday). The Hanja <b class=\"hl\">金 = 금</b> “gold” begins Friday, just like “Fri.”</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 목=木, 토=土, 수=水 — the other days are written differently.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">금</b>요일 = Friday is the debut day of Glowsis!</div></div></div>\n</div>\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-3] Reading — Date format (월/일)</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Read the date and choose the correct reading.</div><div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">제 생일은 5월 17일이에요.</span></div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u4q3\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>오월 십칠일<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>May 17th = 오월 십칠일<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 오=5월, 십칠=17</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>오월 이십일일<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>오월 십일일<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u4q3\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Dates are <b class=\"hl\">Sino-Korean</b>: month = <span class=\"pt-ko\">오월</span> (5월) and day = <span class=\"pt-ko\">십칠일</span> (17일 = 10+7).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">이십일</b> = 21, <b class=\"hl\">십일</b> = 11 — wrong numbers.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Month and day always use Sino numbers: <b class=\"hl\">5월 17일 = 오월 십칠일</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-4] Reading — 언제 (when) for dates</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">A friend asks about your schedule. Choose the best answer.</div><div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">음악방송이 언제예요?</span> <span class=\"pt-ko\">— 금요일이에요.</span></div><div class=\"p-q\">What does the reply tell you?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u4q4\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>It’s on Friday.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ The reply names the day: 금요일이에요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>It’s May 20th.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>It’s 8 o’clock.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>It’s not on Friday.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u4q4\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">언제</b> = “when.” The answer <span class=\"pt-ko\">금요일이에요</span> = “It’s Friday,” naming a day of the week.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The other answers give a date, a time, or a negation — none of which match the reply.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 “언제예요?” can be answered with a <b class=\"hl\">day, a date, or a time</b> — whatever tells “when.”</div></div></div>\n</div>\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-5] Listening — What time is it?</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose the time you hear.</div><button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('지금 두 시 십오 분이에요.')\">🔊 Listen</button><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u4q5\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>두 시 십오 분 = 2:15<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 두 시 십오 분</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>두 시 오 분 = 2:05<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>세 시 십오 분 = 3:15<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>두 시 오십 분 = 2:50<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u4q5\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard <span class=\"pt-ko\">두 시 십오 분</span> = <b class=\"hl\">2:15</b>. The hour <b class=\"hl\">두</b> is a native number; the minutes <b class=\"hl\">십오</b> (15) are Sino.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 오 분 = 5 minutes, 세 시 = 3 o’clock, 오십 분 = 50 minutes — none match.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">몇 시예요?</b> = “What time?” Answer with native hour + Sino minutes.</div></div></div>\n</div>\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-6] Reading — The 한/두/세/네 hour shift</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the natural spoken Korean for each time.</div><div class=\"p-q\">It is 4 o’clock. Which sounds natural?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u4q6\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>넷 시예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>사 시예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>네 시예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ Before 시, 넷 → 네</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>일곱 시예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u4q6\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Before the hour word <b class=\"hl\">시</b>, the native numbers for 1–4 shorten: 하나→<b class=\"hl\">한</b>, 둘→<b class=\"hl\">두</b>, 셋→<b class=\"hl\">세</b>, 넷→<b class=\"hl\">네</b>. So 4 o’clock = <span class=\"pt-ko\">네 시</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">넷 시</b> keeps the full form (wrong before 시); <b class=\"hl\">사 시</b> is the Sino number for 4.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Hours 1–4 shift to <b class=\"hl\">한 두 세 네</b> + 시; hours 5–12 keep their full native form (다섯 여섯…).</div></div></div>\n</div>\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-7] Reading — Order of the week</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct day that follows.</div><div class=\"p-passage\">월 → 화 → 수 → 목 → 금 → ?</div><div class=\"p-q\">Which day comes after 금요일?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u4q7\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>월요일<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>화요일<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>목요일<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>토요일<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ After Fri (금) comes Sat (토)</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u4q7\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The week runs <span class=\"pt-ko\">월 화 수 목 금 토 일</span>. After <b class=\"hl\">금요일</b> (Fri) comes <b class=\"hl\">토요일</b> (Sat).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 월=Mon, 화=Tue, 목=Thu — already passed in the sequence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Remember the order with the classic chant: <b class=\"hl\">월화수목금토일</b>!</div></div></div>\n</div>\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-8] Listening — Asking about a birthday</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Listen to the question and choose the correct reply.</div><button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('생일이 언제예요?')\">🔊 Listen</button><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u4q8\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>오월 십칠일이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ A date answers “when is your birthday”</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>금요일이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>두 시예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>네, 좋아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u4q8\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The question <span class=\"pt-ko\">생일이 언제예요?</span> = “When is your birthday?” The natural reply names a <b class=\"hl\">date</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">오월 십칠일</span> (May 17).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ A day or a clock time answers a different “when”; 좋아요 means “I like it.”</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">생일 = birthday</b>. Answer “언제” for a birthday with month + day.</div></div></div>\n</div>\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-9] Reading — 아침 / 밤 (morning / night)</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div><div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 아침에 운동해요. 밤에는 노래를 불러요.</span></div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u4q9\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>I exercise in the morning and sing at night.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 아침 = morning, 밤 = night</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>I sing in the morning and exercise at night.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>I exercise in the afternoon.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>I sleep all day.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u4q9\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">아침에</b> = “in the morning,” <b class=\"hl\">밤에는</b> = “at night.” So the sentence = “I exercise in the morning and sing at night.”</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Option 2 swaps the two activities; afternoon/조금 are not mentioned.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">아침 ↔ 밤</b> = morning vs night. Use <b class=\"hl\">~에</b> for “at/in” a time.</div></div></div>\n</div>\n"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4-10] Listening — Day + time together</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what matches.</div><button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('데뷔 무대는 금요일 아침 여덟 시예요.')\">🔊 Listen</button><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u4q10\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q10',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>Saturday at 8 pm.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q10',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>Friday at 7 am.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q10',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>Friday at 8 am.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 금요일 = Friday, 여덟 시 = 8 o’clock</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u4q10',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>Sunday at 8 am.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u4q10\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard <span class=\"pt-ko\">금요일 아침 여덟 시</span> = <b class=\"hl\">Friday, 8 in the morning</b>. <b class=\"hl\">금요일</b>=Friday, <b class=\"hl\">여덟 시</b>=8 o’clock.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 토=Sat, 일=Sun, and “7” would be 일곱 시 — none fit.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Chain the day then the time: <b class=\"hl\">[요일] + [시간]</b>, e.g. 금요일 아침 여덟 시.</div></div></div>\n</div>\n"},{"cls":"culture","html":"<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Debut Day = Festival Day!</h3>\n    <p>An idol's <b>debut day (anniversary)</b> is the most special day for fans! They celebrate it like a <b>birthday</b>.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">🎂 On your favorite idol's birthday, fans say: \"생일 축하해요!\" (Happy birthday!)</div>\n  </div>\n\n<!-- ============================================================\n     UNIT 5 — LIKES & DAILY ACTIONS\n     ============================================================ -->"}]},{"id":5,"sections":[{"cls":"unit-flag","html":"<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 5 · LIKES & DAILY ACTIONS</div>\n  "},{"cls":"sec-title","html":"<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">5</div><div><h2>I Like Singing</h2><div class=\"en\">노래를 좋아해요 — Likes · 을/를 · -아요/어요</div></div></div>\n  "},{"cls":"story","html":"<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/story/u5.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 5/8</span>\n      <h3>다희의 좋아하는 것 — \"노래를 좋아해요!\"</h3>\n      <p>대기실 인터뷰! <b>다희</b>는 한국어로 좋아하는 것을 말하는 법을 가르쳐요. \"저는 ○○을 좋아해요!\" — 좋아하는 것을 말할 때마다 음표가 반짝여요. 🎶</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">A waiting-room interview! <b>Dahee</b> teaches how to say what you like in Korean. \"저는 ○○을 좋아해요!\" (I like ○○!) — every time you say what you like, the music notes sparkle. 🎶</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">🎶 GLOW POINT 5/8 획득 — Likes!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"},{"cls":"goals","html":"<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">❤️</span> 좋아해요 (like) / 싫어해요 (dislike)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🔤</span> 을/를 object particle</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🎵</span> -아요/어요 present tense</div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"dialog","html":"<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 5 — Things We Like</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎶 Waiting room interview</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 춤을 좋아해요. 그리고 노래도 좋아해요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I like dancing. And I like singing too.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 랩을 좋아해요. 하지만 매운 음식은 싫어해요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I like rap. But I don't like spicy food.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 팬들을 좋아해요! 팬들이 제일 좋아요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I like our fans! Fans are the best!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 게임을 좋아해요. 매일 밤 게임을 해요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I like games. I play games every night!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">을/를 — Object particle</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">It marks the object of an action. After a final consonant use <b>을</b>, after a vowel use <b>를</b>.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">노래<b>를</b> 좋아해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">노래 has no final consonant → 를</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">랩<b>을</b> 좋아해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">랩 has final consonant ㅂ → 을</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">물을 마셔요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I drink water.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아요/어요 — Present Tense</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">The polite present form of verbs & adjectives. After vowels ㅏ/ㅗ use <b>-아요</b>, otherwise <b>-어요</b>, and 하다 verbs become <b>-해요</b>!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">좋아하<b>다</b> → 좋아<b>해요</b></span><span class=\"gl\">하다 → 해요 (like)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">가<b>다</b> → 가<b>요</b></span><span class=\"gl\">ㅏ + 아요 = 아요 (go)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">먹<b>다</b> → 먹<b>어요</b></span><span class=\"gl\">eat</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">마시<b>다</b> → 마셔요</span><span class=\"gl\">drink</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n    "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-고 싶어요 — \"I want to ~\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Drop 다 from a verb and add <b>-고 싶어요</b> to say what you want to do. A TOPIK I favorite!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">노래하<b>고 싶어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I want to sing.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">춤추<b>고 싶어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I want to dance.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">팬들을 만나<b>고 싶어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I want to meet the fans.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"},{"cls":"teach","html":"<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">&#x1F9D1;&#x200D;&#x1F3EB; Teacher's Deep-Dive &middot; Saying what you like: &#xc744;/&#xb97c; + -&#xc544;&#xc694;/-&#xc5b4;&#xc694; + -&#xace0; &#xc2f6;&#xc5b4;&#xc694;</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">&#xc800;&#xb294; &#xcee4;&#xd53c;&#xb97c; &#xc88b;&#xc544;&#xd574;&#xc694;.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"I like coffee.\" &#x2014; broken down word by word</span></div>\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\"><div class=\"t-why\">Three building blocks in one sentence &#x2014; the topic &#xc800;&#xb294;, the object particle &#xc744;/&#xb97c;, and the present-tense ending -&#xc544;&#xc694;/-&#xc5b4;&#xc694;. How do they fit together?</div>\n  <div class=\"t-deep\">&#xc800;&#xb294; = \"as for me\" (topic, Unit 1). Then <b>&#xcee4;&#xd53c;</b> (coffee) is what you like, so it needs the <b>object particle &#xb97c;</b>. Finally <b>&#xc88b;&#xc544;&#xd574;&#xc694;</b> = <b>&#xc88b;&#xc544;&#xd558;&#xb2e4;</b> (to like) conjugated into polite present. Korean word order is <b>Subject &#x2192; Object &#x2192; Verb</b> &#x2014; the verb always comes LAST. English says \"I like coffee\"; Korean says \"I <i>coffee</i> like.\"</div></div>\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\"><div class=\"t-word\">&#xc800;&#xb294;</div><div class=\"t-role\">I / as for me<span class=\"t-sub\">(topic)</span></div><div class=\"t-note\">from Unit 1's &#xc740;/&#xb294; &#x2014; sets the subject</div></div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-qcell\"><div class=\"t-word\">&#xcee4;&#xd53c;&#xb97c;</div><div class=\"t-role\">coffee<span class=\"t-sub\">(object &#xb97c;)</span></div><div class=\"t-note\">&#xcee4;&#xd53c; ends in a vowel &#2192; <b>&#xb97c;</b></div></div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\"><div class=\"t-word\">&#xc88b;&#xc544;&#xd574;&#xc694;</div><div class=\"t-role\">like<span class=\"t-sub\">(&#xd558;&#xb2e4; &#8594; &#xd574;&#xc694;)</span></div><div class=\"t-note\">&#xc88b;&#xc544;&#xd558;&#xb2e4; &#8594; &#xc88b;&#xc544;<b>&#xd574;</b>&#xc694;</div></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"t-insight\"><b class=\"t-i-ko\">&#xc744;/&#xb97c; rule:</b> look at the <b>last letter</b> of the noun &#x2014; a <b>&#xbc1b;&#xce68;</b> (final consonant) &#8594; <b>&#xc744;</b>; a <b>vowel</b> &#8594; <b>&#xb97c;</b>. So <b>&#xbb3c;&#xc744;</b> (&#xbc1b;&#xce68; &#x3139;), <b>&#xc74c;&#xc545;&#xc744;</b> (&#xbc1b;&#xce68; &#x3131;), but <b>&#xcee4;&#xd53c;&#xb97c;</b> (vowel).</div>\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>&#xbc1b;&#xce68; &#8594; &#xc744;</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">&#xbb3c;&#xc744; &#xb9c8;&#xc154;&#xc694; &#xb7a9;&#xc744; &#xc88b;&#xc544;&#xd574;&#xc694; &#xc74c;&#xc545;&#xc744; &#xb4e4;&#xc5b4;&#xc694;</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">noun ends in a consonant &#8594; &#xc744;</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Vowel &#8594; &#xb97c;</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">&#xcee4;&#xd53c;&#xb97c; &#xc88b;&#xc544;&#xd574;&#xc694; &#xb178;&#xb798;&#xb97c; &#xd574;&#xc694; &#xac8c;&#xc784;&#xc744; &#xd574;&#xc694;</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">noun ends in a vowel &#8594; &#xb97c;</span></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">&#x1F4A1; <b>Memory trick:</b> for the ending, -&#xc544;&#xc694;/-&#xc5b4;&#xc694; is the friendly present form (&#xc0ac;&#xb791; = polite &#xc694;). Verbs keep it simple: vowels <b>&#xc544;/&#xc624;</b> &#8594; <b>-&#xc544;&#xc694;</b> (&#xac00;&#xb2e4; &#8594; &#xac00;&#xc694;), all others &#8594; <b>-&#xc5b4;&#xc694;</b> (&#xba39;&#xb2e4; &#8594; &#xba39;&#xc5b4;&#xc694;), and <b>&#xd558;&#xb2e4;</b> verbs &#8594; <b>-&#xd574;&#xc694;</b> (&#xc88b;&#xc544;&#xd558;&#xb2e4; &#8594; &#xc88b;&#xc544;&#xd574;&#xc694;). Want to <b>want</b> something? Just do verb-stem + <b>-&#xace0; &#xc2f6;&#xc5b4;&#xc694;</b>: <b>&#xac00;&#xace0; &#xc2f6;&#xc5b4;&#xc694;</b> = \"I want to go.\"</div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"vocab-lab","html":"<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">💗</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">좋아함 & 감정<small>Likes & Feelings · 좋아하다 • 싫어하다</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_like.webp\" alt=\"좋아하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('좋아해요')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">좋아하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">joahada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to like</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_dislike.webp\" alt=\"싫어하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('싫어해요')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">싫어하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sireohada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to dislike</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어들로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 춤을 좋아해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 춤을 좋아해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I like dancing.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 랩을 좋아해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 랩을 좋아해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I like rap.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('매운 음식을 싫어해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">매운 음식을 싫어해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I dislike spicy food.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('팬들을 좋아해요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">팬들을 좋아해요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I like (our) fans!</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">📎 <b>좋아하다</b>(like) and <b>싫어하다</b>(dislike) are an opposite pair. Both are <b>하다</b> verbs, so they become <b>좋아해요</b> / <b>싫어해요</b> in polite speech — just like 노래하다 → 노래해요!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎤</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">노래 & 춤<small>Songs & Dance · 노래하다 • 춤 • 노래방</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_sing.webp\" alt=\"노래하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('노래해요')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">노래하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">noraehada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to sing</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_dance.webp\" alt=\"춤\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('춤')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">춤</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chum</div><div class=\"vw-en\">dance</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_noraebang.webp\" alt=\"노래방\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('노래방')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">노래방</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">noraebang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">karaoke room</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어들로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('노래를 좋아해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">노래를 좋아해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I like singing.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('춤을 추고 싶어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">춤을 추고 싶어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I want to dance.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('노래방에 가고 싶어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">노래방에 가고 싶어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I want to go to a noraebang.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('노래방에서 노래해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">노래방에서 노래해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I sing at the karaoke room.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">📎 <b>노래</b>(song) + <b>방</b>(room) = <b>노래방</b>. And watch the object pairs: <b>춤을 추다</b> (to dance) · <b>노래를 하다</b> (to sing) — the noun always takes 을/를.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🏃</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">일상 활동<small>Daily Activities · 공부‧자‧먹‧운동‧여행‧게임</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">6</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_study.webp\" alt=\"공부하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('공부해요')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">공부하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gongbuhada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to study</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_sleep.webp\" alt=\"자다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('자요')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">자다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to sleep</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_eat.webp\" alt=\"먹다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('먹어요')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">먹다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">meokda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to eat</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_exercise.webp\" alt=\"운동\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('운동해요')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">운동</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">undong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">exercise</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_travel.webp\" alt=\"여행\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('여행해요')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">여행</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeohaeng</div><div class=\"vw-en\">travel</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_game.webp\" alt=\"게임\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('게임')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">게임</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">geim</div><div class=\"vw-en\">game</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어들로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('한국어를 공부해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">한국어를 공부해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I study Korean.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('밤에 일찍 자요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">밤에 일찍 자요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I sleep early at night.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아침에 김밥을 먹어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아침에 김밥을 먹어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I eat kimbap in the morning.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('매일 운동을 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">매일 운동을 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I exercise every day.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('방학에 여행을 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">방학에 여행을 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I travel during vacation.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('친구와 게임을 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">친구와 게임을 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I play games with friends.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">📎 <b>여행</b> pairs with <b>가다</b> (여행을 가요), <b>운동</b> with <b>하다</b> (운동을 해요) — like ‘go on a trip’ / ‘do exercise’ in English. <b>공부하다</b>, <b>자다</b>, <b>먹다</b> are the core daily-verb trio.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🍴</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">음식 & 음료<small>Food & Drink · 음식 • 물 • 커피</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_food.webp\" alt=\"음식\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('음식')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">음식</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eumsik</div><div class=\"vw-en\">food</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_water.webp\" alt=\"물\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('물')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">물</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">mul</div><div class=\"vw-en\">water</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_coffee.webp\" alt=\"커피\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('커피')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">커피</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">keopi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">coffee</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어들로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('한국 음식을 좋아해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">한국 음식을 좋아해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I like Korean food.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('물을 마셔요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">물을 마셔요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I drink water.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('커피를 마시고 싶어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">커피를 마시고 싶어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I want to drink coffee.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아침에 커피를 마셔요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아침에 커피를 마셔요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I drink coffee in the morning.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">📎 <b>음식</b> · <b>물</b> · <b>커피</b> are all objects, so they take 을/를: <b>물을</b> (receives 을), but <b>커피를</b> (receives 를) — watch the 받침!</div></div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-1] Reading &#8212; Object Particle &#xc744;/&#xb97c;</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct object particle &#xc744; or &#xb97c;.</div><div class=\"p-q\">&#xc800;&#xb294; &#xcee4;&#xd53c;(    ) &#xc88b;&#xc544;&#xd574;&#xc694;.</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u5q1\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>을<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>를<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 커피 ends in vowel 이 → 를</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>은<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>에<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u5q1\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">&#x1F9D1;&#x200D;&#x1F3EB; &#xc120;&#xc0dd;&#xb2d8; &#xb178;&#xd2b8; &middot; &#xbb38;&#xc81c; &#xd574;&#xc124;</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><b>커피</b> (coffee) ends in the vowel <b>이</b> — no 받침 → use <b>를</b>. Rule of thumb: last letter is a consonant (받침) → 을; last letter is a vowel → 를. 은 is the topic particle and 에 marks place/time, neither fits an object.</div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-2] Reading &#8212; &#xc744; with a final consonant</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct object particle.</div><div class=\"p-q\">&#xc800;&#xb294; &#xae40;&#xbc25;(    ) &#xc88b;&#xc544;&#xd574;&#xc694;.</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u5q2\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>를<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>을<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 김밥 ends in 받침 ㅂ → 을</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>는<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>가<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u5q2\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">&#x1F9D1;&#x200D;&#x1F3EB; &#xc120;&#xc0dd;&#xb2d8; &#xb178;&#xd2b8; &middot; &#xbb38;&#xc81c; &#xd574;&#xc124;</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><b>김밥</b> (kimbap) ends in the 받침 <b>ㅡ</b> → use <b>을</b>. Compare: 물<b>을</b> (받침 ㄹ), 노래<b>를</b> (vowel). Always check the LAST letter of the noun before choosing.</div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-3] Listening &#8212; What Does She Like?</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what the speaker likes.</div><button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 노래를 좋아해요.')\">🔊 Listen</button><div class=\"p-q\">뭐를 좋아해요?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u5q3\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>춤을 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>노래를 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ you heard 노래를</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>게임을 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>커피를 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u5q3\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">&#x1F9D1;&#x200D;&#x1F3EB; &#xc120;&#xc0dd;&#xb2d8; &#xb178;&#xd2b8; &middot; &#xbb38;&#xc81c; &#xd574;&#xc124;</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\">The audio says <b>노래를 좋아해요</b> (I like singing). The other options just swap in a different object noun. Listen for the object — here <b>노래</b> — and its particle 를 (vowel ending).</div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-4] Reading &#8212; &#xd558;&#xb2e4; &#8594; &#xd574;&#xc694;</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">&#xd558;&#xb2e4; verbs all soften the same way. Choose the polite present form.</div><div class=\"p-q\">좋아하다 &#8594; ? (polite present)</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u5q4\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>좋아하요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>좋아해요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 하다 → 해요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>좋아요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>좋아했어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u5q4\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">&#x1F9D1;&#x200D;&#x1F3EB; &#xc120;&#xc0dd;&#xb2d8; &#xb178;&#xd2b8; &middot; &#xbb38;&#xc81c; &#xd574;&#xc124;</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\">Every <b>하다</b> verb becomes <b>해요</b> in polite present: 좋아하다 → 좋아해요, 공부하다 → 공부해요, 노래하다 → 노래해요. Beware 좋아요 — that’s the adjective 좋다 (to be good), a different word.</div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-5] Reading &#8212; -&#xc544;&#xc694;/-&#xc5b4;&#xc694; Present</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct polite present form of the verb.</div><div class=\"p-q\">자다 (to sleep) &#8594; ?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u5q5\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>자요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ stem 자 + 아요 → 자요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>자아요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>자어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>잡아요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u5q5\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">&#x1F9D1;&#x200D;&#x1F3EB; &#xc120;&#xc0dd;&#xb2d8; &#xb178;&#xd2b8; &middot; &#xbb38;&#xc81c; &#xd574;&#xc124;</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\">자다 → stem <b>자</b>. After vowel <b>아/오</b> we add <b>-아요</b>: 자 + 아요 → 자아요, but the two 아’s merge to give <b>자요</b> (가다 → 가요 the same way). Other vowels take -어요, e.g. 먹다 → 먹어요.</div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-6] Listening &#8212; &#x2014;&#xace0; &#xc2f6;&#xc5b4;&#xc694;</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what the speaker wants to do.</div><button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('한국에 가고 싶어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button><div class=\"p-q\">뭐를 하고 싶어요?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u5q6\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>한국에 가고 싶어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ I want to go to Korea</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>한국에서 자고 싶어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>한국에 가고 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>한국에 갔어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u5q6\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">&#x1F9D1;&#x200D;&#x1F3EB; &#xc120;&#xc0dd;&#xb2d8; &#xb178;&#xd2b8; &middot; &#xbb38;&#xc81c; &#xd574;&#xc124;</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\">The audio is <b>가고 싶어요</b> (I want to go). <b>-고 싶어요</b> = “I want to ~” (verb stem + 고 싶어요). 가고 있어요 means “I am going” (progressive), not “want.”</div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-7] Reading &#8212; &#x2014;&#xace0; &#xc2f8;&#xc5b4;&#xc694; connector</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Choose what completes the -&#xace0; &#xc2f8;&#xc5b4;&#xc694; expression.</div><div class=\"p-q\">&#xc800;&#xb294; &#xcee4;&#xd53c;&#xb97c; &#xb9c8;&#xc2dc;(    ) &#xc2f8;&#xc5b4;&#xc694;.</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u5q7\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>고<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 마시다 → 마시고 싶어요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>기<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>어<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u5q7\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">&#x1F9D1;&#x200D;&#x1F3EB; &#xc120;&#xc0dd;&#xb2d8; &#xb178;&#xd2b8; &middot; &#xbb38;&#xc81c; &#xd574;&#xc124;</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\">마시다 (to drink) → drop 다, add <b>고 싶어요</b> → <b>마시고 싶어요</b> = “I want to drink.” The connector is always <b>고</b>: verb-stem + 고 싶어요.</div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-8] Listening &#8212; What Does He Dislike?</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what the speaker dislikes.</div><button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 매운 음식을 싫어해요.')\">🔊 Listen</button><div class=\"p-q\">뭐를 싫어해요?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u5q8\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>매운 음식<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ you heard 싫어해요 + 매운 음식</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>한국 음식<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>커피<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>노래방<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u5q8\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">&#x1F9D1;&#x200D;&#x1F3EB; &#xc120;&#xc0dd;&#xb2d8; &#xb178;&#xd2b8; &middot; &#xbb38;&#xc81c; &#xd574;&#xc124;</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\">싫어하다 (to dislike) → <b>싫어해요</b>. The audio says 저는 <b>매운 음식을</b> 싫어해요 = “I dislike spicy food.” 싫어해요 is the exact opposite of 좋아해요.</div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-9] Reading &#8212; Reading a Fan Message</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Read Dahee’s message and choose what she likes most.</div><div class=\"p-q\">다희: 저는 노래를 좋아해요. 춤도 좋아해요. 하지만 매운 음식은 싫어해요. &#8212; 다희는 뭐를 좋아해요?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u5q9\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>노래와 춤<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ she likes singing and dancing</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>매운 음식<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>노래방에 가는 것<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>게임<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u5q9\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">&#x1F9D1;&#x200D;&#x1F3EB; &#xc120;&#xc0dd;&#xb2d8; &#xb178;&#xd2b8; &middot; &#xbb38;&#xc81c; &#xd574;&#xc124;</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\">Dahee says 노래를 좋아해요 and 춤<b>도</b> 좋아해요 (“also likes dance” — <b>도</b> = also/too), but 매운 음식은 싫어해요 (dislikes). So she likes both singing and dancing.</div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\"><div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5-10] Listening &#8212; Full-Sentence Recap</span></div><div class=\"p-dir\">Listen to the full sentence and choose its meaning.</div><button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('토요일에 운동을 하고 싶어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button><div class=\"p-q\">들은 문장의 뜻은?</div><div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u5q10\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>I want to exercise on Saturday.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 토요일 = Saturday, 운동을 하고 싶어요 = want to do exercise</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>I do exercise on Sunday.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>I don’t like exercise.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u5q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>I’m exercising now.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div><div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u5q10\"></div><div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">&#x1F9D1;&#x200D;&#x1F3EB; &#xc120;&#xc0dd;&#xb2d8; &#xb178;&#xd2b8; &middot; &#xbb38;&#xc81c; &#xd574;&#xc124;</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\">토요일에 = on Saturday · 운동을 = exercise (object, 받침 ㅇ → 을) · 하고 싶어요 = want to do. Full meaning: “I want to exercise on Saturday.” Watch the day (토요일, Sat) and the -<b>고 싶어요</b> want-ending.</div></div></div>"},{"cls":"culture","html":"<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Essential Idol Interview Question</h3>\n    <p>A question you hear often in interviews: <b>\"뭐를 좋아해요?\"</b> (What do you like?) — Introduce your 최애 (ultimate favorite) idol!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">💖 최애 = your absolute favorite thing/person. \"제 최애는 꿈아란에요!\" — fan language!</div>\n  </div>\n\n<!-- ============================================================\n     UNIT 6 — FOOD\n     ============================================================ -->"}]},{"id":6,"sections":[{"cls":"unit-flag","html":"<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 6 · FOOD</div>\n  "},{"cls":"sec-title","html":"<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">6</div><div><h2>Tteokbokki is Spicy</h2><div class=\"en\">떡볶이는 매워요 — Food · 안/못</div></div></div>\n  "},{"cls":"story","html":"<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/story/u6.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 6/8</span>\n      <h3>아란의 맛있는 휴게소 — \"떡볶이는 매워요!\"</h3>\n      <p><b>아란</b>은 한국 음식에 푹 빠졌어요 — 떡볶이, 김밥, 치킨! <b>맛을 말하는 법</b>을 알면 팬들에게 한국 음식을 소개할 수 있어요. \"맛있어요!\" 🍜</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\"><b>Aran</b> has fallen for Korean food — tteokbokki, gimbap, chicken! If you know how to <b>describe taste</b>, you can introduce Korean food to fans. \"맛있어요!\" (It's delicious!) 🍜</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">🍜 GLOW POINT 6/8 획득 — Food & Taste!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"},{"cls":"goals","html":"<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🍜</span> Food vocabulary</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">😋</span> Taste adjectives</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🚫</span> 안 + verb (negation)</div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"dialog","html":"<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 6 — Spicy Food</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🍽️ Eating at the rest stop</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">떡볶이 먹어요? 맛있어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Want to eat tteokbokki? It's delicious!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">떡볶이는 매워요. 저는 매운 음식을 안 먹어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Tteokbokki is spicy. I don't eat spicy food.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">김밥은 안 매워요. 김밥 먹어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Gimbap isn't spicy. Let's eat gimbap!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 저는 김밥을 좋아해요. 맛있어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Great! I like gimbap. It's delicious!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">Taste Expressions — Adjectives</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">A TOPIK I food-question favorite! Use adjectives to describe taste.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">맛있어요 / 맛없어요</span><span class=\"gl\">delicious / not tasty</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">매워요 / 안 매워요</span><span class=\"gl\">spicy / not spicy</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">달아요 / 짜요 / 시어요</span><span class=\"gl\">sweet / salty / sour</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">따뜻해요 / 차가워요</span><span class=\"gl\">warm / cold</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">안 + Verb — Negation</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Put <b>안</b> before a verb/adjective to say \"don't ~\". <b>못</b> means \"can't\" (lack of ability).</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">매운 음식을 <b>안</b> 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I don't eat spicy food.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 노래를 <b>못</b> 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can't sing.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">오늘은 <b>안</b> 추워요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It's not cold today.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n    "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">못 + verb — \"can't ~\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>안</b> = \"don't\" (choice), <b>못</b> = \"can't\" (no ability). Both go before the verb. Compare: 안 먹어요 vs 못 먹어요!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 매운 음식을 <b>못</b> 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can't eat spicy food.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">오늘은 운동을 <b>못</b> 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can't exercise today.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">노래를 <b>못</b> 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can't sing.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"},{"cls":"teach","html":"<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Taste words are irregular — 매워요, not 맵아요!</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">떡볶이는 매워요!</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= &quot;Tteokbokki is spicy!&quot; — so why not 맵아요?</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Why Korean sounds like this — taste words do NOT just take a plain ~아/어요 ending.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      <b>맵다</b> (to be spicy) ends in the consonant <b>ㅂ</b>. When you add the polite ending, that <b>ㅂ isn't kept</b> —\n      it changes into <b>워</b>, giving <b>매워요</b>. Koreans never say &quot;맵아요&quot; — they say <b>매워요</b>. Most taste words are irregular like this!\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">맵다 → 매워요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">spicy <span class=\"t-sub\">(ㅂ-irregular)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Final <b>ㅂ</b> → <b>워</b><br>맵 + 어요 = <b>매워요</b></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">달다 → 달아요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">sweet <span class=\"t-sub\">(ㄹ-irregular)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Final <b>ㄹ</b> drops<br>달 + 아요 = <b>달아요</b></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">짜다 → 짜요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">salty <span class=\"t-sub\">(regular)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>ㅏ</b> stem merges<br>짜 + 아요 = <b>짜요</b></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-qcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">맛있다 → 맛있어요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">delicious <span class=\"t-sub\">(special)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">있다 → 있어요<br>NOT &quot;맛맛다&quot;</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    And when a food <b>doesn't</b> have that taste, put <b>안</b> right before the adjective:\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">안 매워요</b> (not spicy), <b class=\"t-i-ko\">안 짜요</b> (not salty). There's a second negative too — 안 vs 못!\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>안 = &quot;don't / won't&quot;</b> — my choice<br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 매운 음식을 <b>안</b> 먹어요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">I choose not to eat spicy food.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>못 = &quot;can't&quot;</b> — no ability<br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 매운 음식을 <b>못</b> 먹어요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">I am unable to eat spicy food.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> <b>안</b> = my decision (I won't), <b>못</b> = my limit (I can't). If it's too spicy to eat → <b>못</b>. If you just don't want it → <b>안</b>!</div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"vocab-lab","html":"<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🌶️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">매운 한국 음식<small>Spicy Korean food · 떡볶이 김밥 라면 만두 치킨</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">5</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_tteokbokki.webp\" alt=\"떡볶이\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('떡볶이')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">떡볶이</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">tteokbokki</div><div class=\"vw-en\">spicy rice cakes</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_gimbap.webp\" alt=\"김밥\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('김밥')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">김밥</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gimbap</div><div class=\"vw-en\">seaweed rice roll</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_ramyeon.webp\" alt=\"라면\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('라면')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">라면</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ramyeon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">instant noodles</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_mandu.webp\" alt=\"만두\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('만두')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">만두</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">mandu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">dumplings</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_chicken.webp\" alt=\"치킨\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('치킨')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">치킨</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chikin</div><div class=\"vw-en\">fried chicken</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('떡볶이는 매워요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">떡볶이는 매워요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Tteokbokki is spicy.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 김밥을 좋아해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 김밥을 좋아해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I like gimbap.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('라면은 좀 짜요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">라면은 좀 짜요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Ramyeon is a little salty.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('만두는 맛있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">만두는 맛있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The dumplings are delicious.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('치킨하고 콜라를 먹어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">치킨하고 콜라를 먹어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I eat fried chicken and drink cola (chimaek!).</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🍽️ <b>한국 음식:</b> 떡볶이·라면은 보통 <b>매워요</b> (spicy), 김밥·만두는 맵지 않아요. 음식을 칭찬할 땐 <b>맛있어요!</b></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🍰</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">간식 & 음료<small>Snacks & drinks · 콜라 빵 과일 케이크</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_cola.webp\" alt=\"콜라\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('콜라')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">콜라</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">kolla</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cola</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_bread.webp\" alt=\"빵\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('빵')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">빵</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ppang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">bread</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_fruit.webp\" alt=\"과일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('과일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">과일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gwail</div><div class=\"vw-en\">fruit</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_cake.webp\" alt=\"케이크\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('케이크')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">케이크</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">keikeu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cake</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('콜라는 달아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">콜라는 달아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Cola is sweet.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 빵은 맛있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 빵은 맛있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">This bread is delicious.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('과일을 매일 먹어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">과일을 매일 먹어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I eat fruit every day.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('생일 케이크는 달아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">생일 케이크는 달아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The birthday cake is sweet.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🥤 <b>단 음식:</b> 콜라·케이크는 <b>달아요</b> (sweet). <b>달다</b>는 ㄹ 불규칙이라 <b>달아요</b>예요!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">😋</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">맛 표현<small>Taste adjectives · 맛있다 맵다 달다 짜다</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_delicious.webp\" alt=\"맛있다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('맛있어요')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">맛있다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">masitda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">delicious</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_spicy.webp\" alt=\"맵다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('매워요')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">맵다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">maepta</div><div class=\"vw-en\">spicy</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_sweet.webp\" alt=\"달다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('달아요')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">달다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">dalda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">sweet</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_salty.webp\" alt=\"짜다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('짜요')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">짜다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jjada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">salty</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('맛있어요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">맛있어요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It's delicious!</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 떡볶이는 너무 매워요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 떡볶이는 너무 매워요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">This tteokbokki is too spicy.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('김치가 좀 짜요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">김치가 좀 짜요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The kimchi is a little salty.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('케이크가 정말 달아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">케이크가 정말 달아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The cake is really sweet.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">😋 <b>맛 말하기:</b> <b>맛있어요</b> (delicious) · <b>매워요</b> (spicy) · <b>달아요</b> (sweet) · <b>짜요</b> (salty). 반대는 <b>맛없어요</b>!</div></div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-1] Reading — choose the meaning of 맛있다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read the sentence and choose what it means.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">이 김밥은 맛있어요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u6q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q1',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span><span class=\"o-txt\">This gimbap is spicy.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q1',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span><span class=\"o-txt\">This gimbap is salty.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q1',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span><span class=\"o-txt\">This gimbap is delicious.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 맛있다 = delicious (맛 taste + 있다 have)</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q1',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span><span class=\"o-txt\">This gimbap is sweet.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u6q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">맛있다</span> means <b class=\"hl\">delicious</b> — 맛 (taste) + 있다 (to have) = &quot;it has great taste&quot;.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ spicy = <b class=\"hl\">매워요</b> · salty = <b class=\"hl\">짜요</b> · sweet = <b class=\"hl\">달아요</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 김밥 is usually mild and tasty, so 맛있어요 is the natural match!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-2] Reading — choose the correct form (맵다 → 매워요)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">맵다 (to be spicy). Choose the correct polite form to complete the sentence.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">떡볶이는 ______.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u6q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q2',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span><span class=\"o-txt\">맵어요</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q2',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span><span class=\"o-txt\">매아요</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q2',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span><span class=\"o-txt\">매버요</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q2',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span><span class=\"o-txt\">매워요</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ㅂ changes to 워 → 매워요</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u6q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">맵다 is a <b class=\"hl\">ㅂ-irregular</b> adjective: the final ㅂ is <b class=\"hl\">not kept</b> — it turns into <b class=\"hl\">워</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">So 맵 + 어요 = <b class=\"hl\">매워요</b>, and &quot;맵어요&quot; is never used.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Same pattern gives 춥다 → 추워요 (cold) too!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-3] Reading — 안 vs 못 (못 먹어요)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the Korean sentence that means &quot;I can't eat chicken (I have no ability).&quot;</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u6q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span><span class=\"o-txt\">치킨을 못 먹어요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 못 = can't (no ability)</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span><span class=\"o-txt\">치킨을 안 먹어요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span><span class=\"o-txt\">치킨이 맛있어요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span><span class=\"o-txt\">치킨을 좋아해요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u6q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">못</b> means <b class=\"hl\">can&apos;t</b> — a lack of ability. <span class=\"pt-ko\">못 먹어요</span> = I can&apos;t eat.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">안 먹어요</b> = I don&apos;t / won&apos;t eat (my own choice).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 If there&apos;s no ability → <b>못</b>; if it&apos;s just a choice → <b>안</b>!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-4] Reading — choose the meaning of 짜다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read the sentence and choose what it means.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">김치가 좀 짜요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u6q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span><span class=\"o-txt\">The kimchi is very sweet.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span><span class=\"o-txt\">The kimchi is a little salty.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 짜요 = salty, 좀 = a little</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span><span class=\"o-txt\">The kimchi is not spicy.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span><span class=\"o-txt\">The kimchi is expensive.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u6q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">짜다</span> = <b class=\"hl\">salty</b>. As a regular ㅏ stem it becomes <b class=\"hl\">짜요</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">좀</b> = a little · sweet = <b class=\"hl\">달아요</b> · spicy = <b class=\"hl\">매워요</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Kimchi is salty and a bit spicy — 짜요 fits it well!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-5] Reading — choose the correct form (달다 → 달아요)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct polite form of 달다 (to be sweet) to complete the sentence.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">케이크가 ______.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u6q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span><span class=\"o-txt\">달라요</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span><span class=\"o-txt\">달어요</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span><span class=\"o-txt\">달아요</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ㄹ drops → 달아요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q5',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span><span class=\"o-txt\">달아해요</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u6q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">달다 is a <b class=\"hl\">ㄹ-irregular</b> adjective: the final <b class=\"hl\">ㄹ drops</b> before 아/어.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">So 달 + 아요 = <b class=\"hl\">달아요</b>. We never say &quot;달라요&quot; for an adjective.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 콜라·케이크 are <b>달아요</b> (sweet)!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-6] Listening — food vocabulary</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the food the person talks about.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 라면을 좋아해요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u6q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span><span class=\"o-txt\">떡볶이</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span><span class=\"o-txt\">치킨</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span><span class=\"o-txt\">라면</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅ they said they like 라면</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q6',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span><span class=\"o-txt\">만두</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u6q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker says <span class=\"pt-ko\">라면을 좋아해요</span> — they like <b class=\"hl\">라면</b> (instant noodles).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 떡볶이·치킨·만두 are other foods, but they weren&apos;t mentioned.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listening for the food noun alone is enough to answer here!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-7] Listening — taste words (매워요)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the sentence that matches what you hear.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('이 떡볶이는 정말 매워요!')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u6q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span><span class=\"o-txt\">이 떡볶이는 달아요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span><span class=\"o-txt\">이 떡볶이는 안 매워요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span><span class=\"o-txt\">이 떡볶이는 짜요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q7',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span><span class=\"o-txt\">이 떡볶이는 정말 매워요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 매워요 = spicy, 정말 = really</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u6q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard <span class=\"pt-ko\">정말 매워요</span> — the tteokbokki is <b class=\"hl\">really spicy</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">정말</b> = really · <b class=\"hl\">달아요</b>=sweet · <b class=\"hl\">짜요</b>=salty.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Catch the taste word <b>매워요</b> — the ㅂ-irregular form!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-8] Listening — 안 negation (choice)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what is true about the speaker.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 매운 음식을 안 먹어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u6q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span><span class=\"o-txt\">매운 음식을 먹어요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span><span class=\"o-txt\">매운 음식을 안 먹어요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 안 = doesn't (choice)</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span><span class=\"o-txt\">매운 음식을 못 먹어요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span><span class=\"o-txt\">음식을 안 좋아해요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u6q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard <span class=\"pt-ko\">매운 음식을 안 먹어요</span> — the person <b class=\"hl\">doesn&apos;t eat spicy food</b> by choice.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">못 먹어요</b> would mean they <b class=\"hl\">can&apos;t</b> eat it (ability), which wasn&apos;t said.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b>안</b> = I won&apos;t / I choose not to!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-9] Listening — 못 negation (ability)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what is true about the speaker.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 술을 못 마셔요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u6q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span><span class=\"o-txt\">술을 마셔요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span><span class=\"o-txt\">술을 안 마셔요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span><span class=\"o-txt\">술을 못 마셔요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 못 = can't (no ability)</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span><span class=\"o-txt\">술을 좋아해요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u6q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard <span class=\"pt-ko\">술을 못 마셔요</span> — the person <b class=\"hl\">can&apos;t drink</b> alcohol (no ability).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">안 마셔요</b> = doesn&apos;t drink (choice) — different meaning from 못!</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b>못</b> sits before the verb too: 못 + 마셔요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6-10] Listening — ordering at a restaurant</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 At the restaurant, Aran says one line to the server. What is she doing?</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('떡볶이 하나 주세요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u6q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span><span class=\"o-txt\">음악을 들어요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span><span class=\"o-txt\">떡볶이를 주문해요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 주세요 = polite 'please give me' → ordering</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span><span class=\"o-txt\">노래를 해요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u6q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span><span class=\"o-txt\">김밥을 안 먹어요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u6q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard <span class=\"pt-ko\">떡볶이 하나 주세요</span> — she is <b class=\"hl\">ordering tteokbokki</b> at the restaurant.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">하나</b> = one (of something) · <b class=\"hl\">주세요</b> = &quot;please give me&quot;.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 하늘 <span class=\"pt-ko\">… 주세요</span> is how you order food or anything!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"culture","html":"<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Idol V-Live Mukbang</h3>\n    <p>Idols do <b>mukbang (eating shows)</b> on V LIVE! Fans comment \"맛있게 먹어요!\" (Enjoy your meal!).</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">🍗 Chicken + cola = the chimaek culture! To say what you want: \"치킨 먹고 싶어요\" — you'll learn -고 싶어요 in 1B.</div>\n  </div>\n\n<!-- ============================================================\n     UNIT 7 — LOCATION\n     ============================================================ -->"}]},{"id":7,"sections":[{"cls":"unit-flag","html":"<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 7 · LOCATION</div>\n  "},{"cls":"sec-title","html":"<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">7</div><div><h2>I'm in the Practice Room</h2><div class=\"en\">연습실에 있어요 — Location · 에/에서</div></div></div>\n  "},{"cls":"story","html":"<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/story/u7.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 7/8</span>\n      <h3>채아의 위치 알리기 — \"연습실에 있어요!\"</h3>\n      <p>글로시스 멤버들은 각자 다른 장소에 있어요! <b>채아</b>는 위치를 말하는 법을 배워요 — \"어디에 있어요?\" 장소를 말할수록 멤버들이 모여요. 📍</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">The Glowsis members are all in different places! <b>Chaea</b> learns how to say where she is — \"어디에 있어요?\" (Where are you?). The more places they say, the more members gather. 📍</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">📍 GLOW POINT 7/8 획득 — Locations!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"},{"cls":"goals","html":"<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">📍</span> Where are you?</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🔤</span> 에 / 에서 particles</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🏠</span> Place vocabulary</div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"dialog","html":"<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 7 — Where Are the Members?</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">📱 Group chat</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">지금 어디에 있어요? 연습이에요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Where are you now? It's practice time!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 연습실에 있어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I'm in the practice room!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 집에 있어요. 조금 있어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I'm at home. Wait a bit!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 카페에서 커피를 마셔요. 곧 갈게요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I'm drinking coffee at the cafe. I'll come soon!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">에 — Location & Time</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">N에 = \"at/in ~ (있다/없다)\" — the place where something exists, and also time.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">연습실<b>에</b> 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'm in the practice room.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">집<b>에</b> 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'm at home.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">5월 20일<b>에</b> 데뷔해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">We debut on May 20th. (time)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">에서 — Place of Action</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">N에서 = \"at ~ (do an action)\" — the place where an action happens.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">카페<b>에서</b> 커피를 마셔요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I drink coffee at the cafe.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">연습실에서 춤을 춰요.</span><span class=\"gl\">We dance in the practice room.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">학교에서 공부해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I study at school.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n    "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">위 / 아래 / 옆 / 앞 / 뒤 — position words</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Say where things are: <b>N 위에</b> (above), <b>N 아래에</b> (below), <b>N 옆에</b> (next to), <b>N 앞에</b> (in front), <b>N 뒤에</b> (behind).</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">책상 <b>위에</b> 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It's on top of the desk.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">연습실 <b>옆에</b> 카페가 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">There's a cafe next to the practice room.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">학교 <b>앞에</b> 가게가 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">There's a store in front of the school.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"},{"cls":"teach","html":"<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · 에 vs 에서 — where you ARE vs. where you DO</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">집<b class=\"hl\">에</b> 있어요</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"I'm at home\"</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <span class=\"t-ko\">카페<b class=\"hl\">에서</b> 커피를 마셔요</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"I drink coffee at the cafe\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Both Korean particles translate to \"at\", so WHY do Koreans have two?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      The place is the same — it's the <b>verb</b> that chooses the particle. Existence verbs like\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">있어요 / 없어요</span> (<b>to be, to exist</b>) take <b>에</b>: \"집에 있어요.\" Action verbs — such as\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">마셔요, 먹어요, 춰요, 공부해요</span> — take <b>에서</b> to mark where the action happens: \"카페에서 커피를 마셔요.\"\n      <b>에</b> also marks <b>time</b>: \"5월 20일에 데뷔해요\" (debut on May 20th).\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">N 에</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">at / in <span class=\"t-sub\">(existence + time)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">있어요 / 없어요 + 에.<br>집<b>에</b> 있어요<br>5월 20일<b>에</b> 데뷔해요</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">vs</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-qcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">N 에서</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">at / in <span class=\"t-sub\">(place of action)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Action verb + 에서.<br>카페<b>에서</b> 마셔요<br>연습실<b>에서</b> 춰요</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">Quick trick:</b> Ask <b>\"무엇이 있어요?\"</b> (what exists?) → <b>에</b>. Ask <b>\"뭐 하고 있어요?\"</b> (what are you doing?) → <b>에서</b>.\n    Being somewhere = 에. Doing something somewhere = 에서.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>에 — existence</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">연습실에 있어요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">I'm (I exist) in the practice room.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>에서 — action</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">연습실에서 춤을 춰요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">I dance (I act) in the practice room.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Position words (위 / 아래 / 옆 / 앞 / 뒤):</b> stack them on top of <b>에</b> — N <b>위에</b> = \"on top of\", N <b>옆에</b> = \"next to\".\n    책이 책상 <b>위에</b> 있어요 = \"The book is on the desk.\" These are classic TOPIK I location words to memorize as a set!\n  </div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"vocab-lab","html":"<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎤</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">연습 & 공연<small>Practice & Shows · 연습실/음악방송/콘서트장</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_practiceroom.webp\" alt=\"연습실\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('연습실')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">연습실</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeonseupsil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">practice room</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_musicshow.webp\" alt=\"음악방송\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('음악방송')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">음악방송</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eumakbangsong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">music show</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_concert.webp\" alt=\"콘서트장\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('콘서트장')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">콘서트장</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">konseoteujang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">concert hall</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('연습실에서 춤을 춰요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">연습실에서 춤을 춰요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We dance in the practice room.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('연습실에 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">연습실에 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'm in the practice room.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘 음악방송에 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오늘 음악방송에 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Today I'm at the music show.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('콘서트장에서 노래를 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">콘서트장에서 노래를 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">They sing at the concert hall.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('콘서트장 앞에 사람이 많아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">콘서트장 앞에 사람이 많아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">There are many people in front of the concert hall.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🎶 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> 연습실에서 <b>연습해요</b>, 콘서트장에서 <b>공연해요</b>. 존재는 에(음악방송<b>에</b> 있어요), 동작은 에서(연습실<b>에서</b> 춰요)!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🏠</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">일상 장소<small>Everyday places · 집/카페/학교/가게/병원</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">5</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_home.webp\" alt=\"집\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('집')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">집</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jip</div><div class=\"vw-en\">home</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_cafe.webp\" alt=\"카페\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('카페')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">카페</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">kape</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cafe</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_school.webp\" alt=\"학교\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('학교')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">학교</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hakgyo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">school</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_shop.webp\" alt=\"가게\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가게')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">가게</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gage</div><div class=\"vw-en\">store, shop</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_hospital.webp\" alt=\"병원\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('병원')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">병원</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">byeongwon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">hospital</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('집에 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">집에 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'm at home.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('카페에서 커피를 마셔요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">카페에서 커피를 마셔요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I drink coffee at the cafe.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('학교에서 공부해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">학교에서 공부해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I study at school.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가게에서 물을 사요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">가게에서 물을 사요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I buy water at the store.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('병원 앞에서 만나요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">병원 앞에서 만나요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Let's meet in front of the hospital.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">📌 <b>에/에서 정리:</b> 존재는 <b>에</b>(집에 있어요), 동작은 <b>에서</b>(카페에서 마셔요)!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat \" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🚇</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">교통<small>Transportation · 지하철/버스</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_subway.webp\" alt=\"지하철\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지하철')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">지하철</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jihacheol</div><div class=\"vw-en\">subway</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_bus.webp\" alt=\"버스\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('버스')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">버스</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">beoseu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">bus</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지하철을 타요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">지하철을 타요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I take the subway.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지하철을 타고 콘서트장에 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">지하철을 타고 콘서트장에 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go to the concert hall by subway.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('버스에서 음악을 들어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">버스에서 음악을 들어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I listen to music on the bus.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('버스를 타요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">버스를 타요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I ride the bus.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🚌 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> 교통수단은 <b>타요</b>(ride). 값을 낼 땐 <b>지하철을 내려요</b>, 그리고 가는 곳은 <b>에</b>로: 콘서트장에 <b>가요</b>!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">📍</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">위치<small>Location words · 어디/위/아래/옆</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_where.webp\" alt=\"어디\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어디')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">어디</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eodi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">where</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_above.webp\" alt=\"위\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('위')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">위</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">wi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">above, top</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_below.webp\" alt=\"아래\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아래')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">아래</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">arae</div><div class=\"vw-en\">below, bottom</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_side.webp\" alt=\"옆\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('옆')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">옆</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeop</div><div class=\"vw-en\">next to, side</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어디에 있어요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">어디에 있어요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Where are you?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('책이 책상 위에 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">책이 책상 위에 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The book is on the desk.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('고양이가 침대 아래에 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">고양이가 침대 아래에 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The cat is under the bed.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('콘서트장 옆에 카페가 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">콘서트장 옆에 카페가 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">There's a cafe next to the concert hall.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🗺️ <b>위치 + 에:</b> 위<b>에</b> / 아래<b>에</b> / 옆<b>에</b>. 어디<b>에</b> 있어요? 라고 물으면 — N<b>에</b> 있어요 로 답해요!</div></div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7-1] Reading — Location Blank</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct particle.</div>\n  \n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">아란 씨는 연습실(&nbsp;&nbsp;) 있어요.</span> (Aran is in the practice room.)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u7q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>에서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>에<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 에 = the place something exists; 있어요 is an existence verb</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>을<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>에서 있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u7q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">있어요 / 없어요 are <b class=\"hl\">existence verbs</b>, so the place takes <b class=\"hl\">에</b>: 연습실<b class=\"hl\">에</b> 있어요 (is in the practice room).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">에서</b> = place where an <b>action</b> happens (춤을 춰요). <b class=\"hl\">을</b> = object particle.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Existence → <span class=\"pt-ko\">에</span>. Action → <span class=\"pt-ko\">에서</span>!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7-2] Listening — Where does it happen?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the sentence you heard.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('도서관에서 책을 읽어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  \n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u7q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>책상에서 책을 읽어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>도서관에서 책을 읽어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 도서관에서 + action (읽어요)</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>도서관에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>학교에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u7q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard <span class=\"pt-ko\">도서관에서 책을 읽어요</span>. <b class=\"hl\">읽다</b> (to read) is an action, so the place uses <b class=\"hl\">에서</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">에 있어요</b> means \"to exist there\" — but the sentence is about <b class=\"hl\">doing</b> (reading).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 The ending <b class=\"hl\">-에서</b> (action) vs. <b class=\"hl\">-에 있어요</b> (existence) tells you which is which.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7-3] Reading — Where is it? (picture)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔍 Look at the picture and choose the correct sentence.</div>\n  \n  <div class=\"p-q\"><div class=\"p-passage\">[그림: 책상 <b>위에</b> 책]<span class=\"gl\">[Picture: a book on top of the desk]</span></div></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u7q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>책이 책상 위에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ The book is on the desk. (picture shows it on top)</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>책이 책상 아래에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>책이 책상 옆에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>책이 책상 뒤에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u7q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The picture shows the book <b class=\"hl\">above / on top</b> of the desk → <b class=\"hl\">위에</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">아래에</b>=below, <b class=\"hl\">옆에</b>=next to, <b class=\"hl\">뒤에</b>=behind — none match the picture.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Position words sit <b class=\"hl\">before 에</b>: 위에 / 아래에 / 옆에.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7-4] Reading — Meaning of 에서</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  \n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">학교에서 공부해요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u7q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>I study to school.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>There is a school.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>I study at school.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 공부해요 is an action, so 에서 = \"at school\"</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>The school is big.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u7q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">학교에서</span> = at school, <span class=\"pt-ko\">공부해요</span> = I study. Action verb → <b class=\"hl\">에서</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ \"There is a school\" would be <span class=\"pt-ko\">학교가 있어요</span> (에, not 에서).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">에서 + action verb</b> = the place where you do something.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7-5] Reading — Next to / In front / Behind</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  \n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">연습실 옆에 카페가 있어요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u7q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>The cafe is next to the practice room.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 옆에 = next to</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>The cafe is in front of the practice room.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>The cafe is behind the practice room.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>The cafe is above the practice room.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u7q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">옆에</span> = \"next to / beside\". So the cafe is <b class=\"hl\">next to</b> the practice room.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 앞에=in front, 뒤에=behind, 위에=above — they are <b class=\"hl\">different position words</b>, don't mix them up!</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 A cafe <b class=\"hl\">next to</b> the practice room — perfect for idols after dancing!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7-6] Reading — Where are you?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read the conversation. Fill in the question word.</div>\n  \n  <div class=\"p-q\"><div><span class=\"pt-ko\">로이:</span> 지금(&nbsp;&nbsp;) 있어요? <span class=\"pt-ko\">다희:</span> 연습실에 있어요!</div></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u7q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>어디<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 어디 = where (asking a place)</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>에서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>무엇<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>누구<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u7q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">To ask <b class=\"hl\">where</b> someone is, use <span class=\"pt-ko\">어디</span>: <b class=\"hl\">어디에 있어요?</b> (Where are you?).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">무엇</b>=what, <b class=\"hl\">누구</b>=who. <b class=\"hl\">에서</b> can't start this question alone.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Answer pattern: <span class=\"pt-ko\">연습실에 있어요</span> — N<b class=\"hl\">에</b> 있어요!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7-7] Reading — 에 for time</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  \n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">5월 20일에 데뷔해요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u7q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>We debut on May 20th.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 에 can mark time: on May 20th</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>We debut in the practice room.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>We debut at 5 o'clock 20 times.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>It is May 20th.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u7q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">에</b> marks <b>time</b> as well as location: 5월 20일<b class=\"hl\">에</b> = <b class=\"hl\">on</b> May 20th.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ \"In the practice room\" would be <span class=\"pt-ko\">연습실에서</span>. And \"It is May 20th\" = <span class=\"pt-ko\">5월 20일이에요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 에 = \"at/in/on\" a <b class=\"hl\">place</b> OR a <b class=\"hl\">time</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7-8] Listening — Under the bed</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what you heard about the cat.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('고양이가 침대 아래에 있어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  \n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u7q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>고양이가 책상 아래에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>고양이가 침대 아래에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 침대 아래에 = under the bed</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>고양이가 침대 위에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>고양이가 책상 옆에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u7q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard <span class=\"pt-ko\">침대 아래에 있어요</span> — the cat is <b class=\"hl\">under the bed</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The location word <b class=\"hl\">아래</b> (below) plus the place <span class=\"pt-ko\">침대</span> (bed) are the keys.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Catch the <b class=\"hl\">place + position word</b> first: 침대 아래에 → under the bed.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7-9] Listening — At the music show</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what you heard.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('음악방송에서 노래를 해요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  \n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u7q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>음악방송에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>음악방송에서 노래를 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 음악방송에서 + action (노래를 해요)</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>콘서트장에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>콘서트장에서 노래를 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u7q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard <span class=\"pt-ko\">음악방송에서 노래를 해요</span> — singing is an <b class=\"hl\">action</b>, so 에서.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">에 있어요</b> = existence, not action. The sentence is about <b class=\"hl\">doing</b> (singing).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Music show = <span class=\"pt-ko\">음악방송</span>. Action at a show → <b class=\"hl\">에서</b>!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7-10] Listening — Where are you?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen to the question and choose the best answer.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('지금 어디에 있어요?')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지금 어디에 있어요?</span> (Where are you now?)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u7q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>집에 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ Best answer to \"Where are you?\" is a place + 에 있어요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>커피를 마셔요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>네, 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u7q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>학교입니다.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u7q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">To <span class=\"pt-ko\">어디에 있어요?</span> (Where are you?) the natural answer names a <b class=\"hl\">place + 에 있어요</b>: 집<b class=\"hl\">에</b> 있어요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">커피를 마셔요</b> answers \"what are you doing\", not \"where\". <b class=\"hl\">네, 있어요</b> answers a yes/no existence question.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Where-question → answer with a <b class=\"hl\">place</b>: N<b class=\"hl\">에</b> 있어요!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"culture","html":"<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Places Idols Go</h3>\n    <p><b>Music shows</b> (Music Bank, Inkigayo, M Countdown!), <b>concert halls</b>, <b>fan sign events</b> — an idol's day is all about moving between places!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">🚇 \"음악방송에 어떻게 가요?\" (How do you get to the music show?) — By subway! Transportation comes in 1B!</div>\n  </div>\n\n<!-- ============================================================\n     UNIT 8 — PAST TENSE\n     ============================================================ -->"}]},{"id":8,"sections":[{"cls":"unit-flag","html":"<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 8 · PAST TENSE</div>\n  "},{"cls":"sec-title","html":"<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">8</div><div><h2>What Did You Do Yesterday?</h2><div class=\"en\">어제 뭐 했어요? — Past tense · -았/었어요</div></div></div>\n  "},{"cls":"story","html":"<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/story/u8.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 8/8</span>\n      <h3>마지막 GLOW POINT — \"어제 뭐 했어요?\"</h3>\n      <p>드디어 마지막 포인트! 네 명은 <b>과거 시제</b>로 데뷔 무대의 추억을 이야기해요. \"어제 노래를 불렀어요!\" — 여덟 번째 포인트가 모이면... 데뷔 완성! ✨</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">The final point at last! The four members talk about memories of their debut stage using the <b>past tense</b>. \"어제 노래를 불렀어요!\" (I sang yesterday!) — when the eighth point comes together... debut complete! ✨</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ GLOW POINT 8/8 — DEBUT COMPLETE! → 1B로 계속!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"},{"cls":"goals","html":"<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">⏪</span> -았/었어요 past tense</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">📝</span> Writing a diary</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🎤</span> Life after debut</div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"dialog","html":"<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 8 — The Day After Debut</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🌅 Morning at the dorm</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">어제 정말 재미있었어요! 데뷔 무대, 최고였어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Yesterday was really fun! The debut stage was the best!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">팬들이 많았어요. 저는 정말 감동했어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">There were so many fans. I was really touched.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">우리 노래를 다 같이 불렀어요! 오늘도 힘내요!</div><div class=\"gl\">We all sang our song together! Let's do our best today too!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 어제 치킨을 먹었어요. 맛있었어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I ate fried chicken yesterday. It was delicious!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-았/었어요 — Past Tense</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Change present <b>-아요/어요</b> to <b>-았어요/었어요</b>! After ㅏ/ㅗ → 았어요, otherwise → 었어요, 하다 → 했어요.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">먹<b>다</b> → 먹<b>었어요</b></span><span class=\"gl\">ate</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">하<b>다</b> → <b>했어요</b></span><span class=\"gl\">did</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">재미있<b>다</b> → 재미있<b>었어요</b></span><span class=\"gl\">was fun</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">가<b>다</b> → 갔어요</span><span class=\"gl\">went</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">Time Expressions — 어제/오늘/내일</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">TOPIK I listening always asks \"when?\" Combine time expressions with the past tense!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어제 뭐 했어요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What did you do yesterday?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어제 쇼핑했어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I went shopping yesterday.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">내일 뭐 해요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What are you doing tomorrow?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n    "},{"cls":"grammar","html":"<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">안 + past — \"didn't ~\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Negate the past tense: <b>안</b> + verb (past form). Compare: 했어요 (did) vs 안 했어요 (didn't do).</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어제 공부를 <b>안 했어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I didn't study yesterday.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">아침을 <b>안 먹었어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I didn't eat breakfast.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">음악방송에 <b>안 갔어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I didn't go to the music show.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"},{"cls":"teach","html":"<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Past Tense -았/었어요</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">어제 뭐 했어요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"What did you do yesterday?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Why Korean verbs \"change their tail\" to talk about the past</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      English adds a separate word (<b>\"did\"</b>) — Korean changes the <b>verb's own ending</b>. Present <b>-아요/어요</b> becomes past <b>-았어요/었어요</b>. Which one? Look at the vowel right before it: a bright letter <b class=\"hl\">ㅏ</b> or <b class=\"hl\">ㅗ</b> → <b>았어요</b>; anything else → <b>었어요</b>; and <b>하다</b> is the lucky short form → <b class=\"hl\">했어요</b>.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">가<b>다</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">go <span class=\"t-sub\">(stem 가)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">가 has <b>ㅏ</b><br>→ 가<b>았</b>어요 → <b>갔어요</b></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-qcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">먹<b>다</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">eat <span class=\"t-sub\">(stem 먹)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">먹 has <b>ㅓ</b><br>→ 먹<b>었</b>어요 → <b>먹었어요</b></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">하<b>다</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">do <span class=\"t-sub\">(bonus: X+하다 verbs)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">하다 → <b>했어요</b><br>쇼핑했어요 · 감동했어요</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">\"어제\"</b> (yesterday) is your clue! In TOPIK listening, words like <b>어제 / 그저께</b> flag the past → expect <b>-았/었어요</b>. <b>오늘</b> = present, <b>내일</b> = future.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Past (did)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">어제 공부<b>했어요</b>.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">I studied yesterday.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Negative past (didn't)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">어제 공부를 <b>안 했어요</b>.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">I didn't study yesterday. ✨</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> bright vowels <b>ㅏ/ㅗ</b> grab <b>았</b>, darker vowels (ㅓ/ㅜ/ㅣ) grab <b>었</b>. <b>하다</b> becomes <b>했어요</b> — and since <b>쇼핑하다, 감동하다, 힘내다</b> all end in 하다, their past is simply <b>-했어요</b> too!\n  </div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"vocab-lab","html":"<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">⏰</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">시간<small>Time · 어제/오늘/내일</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_yesterday.webp\" alt=\"어제\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어제')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">어제</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eoje</div><div class=\"vw-en\">yesterday</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_today.webp\" alt=\"오늘\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">오늘</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">oneul</div><div class=\"vw-en\">today</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_tomorrow.webp\" alt=\"내일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('내일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">내일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">naeil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">tomorrow</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어제 뭐 했어요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">어제 뭐 했어요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">What did you do yesterday?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘은 쉬어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오늘은 쉬어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I rest today.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('내일 만나요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">내일 만나요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">See you tomorrow!</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어제 노래를 불렀어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">어제 노래를 불렀어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I sang a song yesterday.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">⏳ <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> <b>어제</b> → past (-았/었어요) · <b>오늘</b> → present · <b>내일</b> → future. \"어제 <b>했어요</b>? ✔\" · \"내일 했어요? ✘\"</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎬</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">주말활동<small>Weekend fun · 영화/쇼핑/드라마/파티</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_movie.webp\" alt=\"영화\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('영화')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">영화</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeonghwa</div><div class=\"vw-en\">movie</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_shopping.webp\" alt=\"쇼핑\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('쇼핑')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">쇼핑</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">syoping</div><div class=\"vw-en\">shopping</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_drama.webp\" alt=\"드라마\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('드라마')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">드라마</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">deurama</div><div class=\"vw-en\">drama</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_party.webp\" alt=\"파티\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('파티')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">파티</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">pati</div><div class=\"vw-en\">party</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어제 영화를 봤어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">어제 영화를 봤어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I watched a movie yesterday.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('주말에 쇼핑했어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">주말에 쇼핑했어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I went shopping on the weekend.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('드라마를 자주 봐요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">드라마를 자주 봐요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I often watch dramas.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('파티를 했어요. 정말 재미있었어요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">파티를 했어요. 정말 재미있었어요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We had a party. It was so fun!</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🎬 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> 영화·드라마는 <b>보다</b> (봤어요), 쇼핑·파티는 <b>하다</b> (했어요). These <b>하다</b> verbs simply become <b>-했어요</b> in the past!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">💕</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">느낌<small>Feelings · 재미있다/감동하다/힘내다</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_fun.webp\" alt=\"재미있다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('재미있다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">재미있다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jaemiitda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">fun, interesting</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_moved.webp\" alt=\"감동하다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('감동하다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">감동하다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gamdonghada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be moved</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_cheer.webp\" alt=\"힘내다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('힘내다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">힘내다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">himnaeda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cheer up</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('콘서트가 정말 재미있었어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">콘서트가 정말 재미있었어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The concert was really fun.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('팬들의 응원에 감동했어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">팬들의 응원에 감동했어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I was moved by the fans' cheers.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('힘내요! 우리가 응원할게요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">힘내요! 우리가 응원할게요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Cheer up! We'll support you!</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">💡 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> 재미있다 → <b>재미있었어요</b> (was fun) · 감동하다 → <b>감동했어요</b> (was moved) · 힘내다 → <b>힘냈어요</b>. Feelings go into the past tense too!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">📍</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">장소<small>Places · 공원/시장/은행</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_park.webp\" alt=\"공원\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('공원')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">공원</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gongwon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">park</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_market.webp\" alt=\"시장\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시장')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">시장</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sijang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">market</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_bank.webp\" alt=\"은행\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('은행')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">은행</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eunhaeng</div><div class=\"vw-en\">bank</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('공원에 갔어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">공원에 갔어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I went to the park.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시장에서 쇼핑했어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">시장에서 쇼핑했어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I went shopping at the market.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('은행에 갔어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">은행에 갔어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I went to the bank.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어제 어디에 갔어요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">어제 어디에 갔어요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Where did you go yesterday?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">📍 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> place + <b>에 가다</b> → 가다(가) has ㅏ → <b>갔어요</b>. \"어디에 갔어요?\" = Where did you go?</div></div></div></div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-1] Reading — Fill in the Blank</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct past tense.</div>\n  \n  <div class=\"p-q\">어제 친구를(    ).</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u8q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>만나요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ present</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>만났어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ met (past)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>만날 거예요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ future</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>만나고 있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ progressive</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u8q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">어제</b> = yesterday → the verb must be <b class=\"hl\">past</b>. <span class=\"pt-ko\">만나다</span> (to meet) → stem <span class=\"pt-ko\">만나</span> ends in ㅏ, so <b class=\"hl\">만났어요</b> (met).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 만나요=present, 만날 거예요=future, 만나고 있어요=progressive — none is past.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Bright vowel <b class=\"hl\">ㅏ/ㅗ</b> takes <b class=\"hl\">았</b> → -았어요!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-2] Listening — What did you do yesterday?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('어제 뭐 했어요?')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  \n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u8q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>네, 좋아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ </span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>어제 영화를 봤어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ watched a movie</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>내일 영화를 봐요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ tomorrow</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>저는 학생이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ </span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u8q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The question <span class=\"pt-ko\">어제 뭐 했어요?</span> asks about <b class=\"hl\">yesterday</b> → the reply needs <b class=\"hl\">past tense with 어제</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">어제 영화를 봤어요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Option 3 says <b class=\"hl\">내일</b> (tomorrow) — wrong time word!</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Catch the time word <b class=\"hl\">어제</b> first; it locks in the past.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-3] Reading — Didn't do</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct negative past tense.</div>\n  \n  <div class=\"p-q\">어제 숙제를(    ).</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u8q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>안 했어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ didn't do (homework)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>안 해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ present</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>했어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ positive</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>할 거예요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ future</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u8q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">안 + past verb</b> = \"didn&#39;t\". <span class=\"pt-ko\">안 했어요</span> = didn&#39;t do → \"I didn&#39;t do homework yesterday.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 안 해요=present, 했어요=positive (did), 할 거예요=future.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Grammar 3: 했어요 (did) ↔ <b class=\"hl\">안 했어요</b> (didn&#39;t do) — just drop <b class=\"hl\">안</b> before the past form!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-4] Reading — 하다 → 했어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct past tense of a 하다 verb.</div>\n  \n  <div class=\"p-q\">어제 쇼핑을(    ).</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u8q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>쇼핑해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ present</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>쇼핑했어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ did shopping (past)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>쇼핑할 거예요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ future</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>쇼핑하고 있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ progressive</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u8q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">쇼핑하다</span> ends in <b class=\"hl\">하다</b> → past is <span class=\"pt-ko\">쇼핑했어요</span>. Every <b class=\"hl\">하다</b> verb becomes <b class=\"hl\">했어요</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 쇼핑해요=present, 쇼핑할 거예요=future, 쇼핑하고 있어요=progressive.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 No vowel rule needed — <b class=\"hl\">하다</b> always → <b class=\"hl\">했어요</b>. 감동했어요, 파티했어요, 힘냈어요!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-5] Reading — ㅏ → 았어요 (가다)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct past tense.</div>\n  \n  <div class=\"p-q\">어제 공원에(    ).</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u8q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>가요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ present</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>갔어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ went (past)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>갈 거예요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ future</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>가고 있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ progressive</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u8q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">가다</span> (to go) → stem <span class=\"pt-ko\">가</span> ends in the bright vowel <b class=\"hl\">ㅏ</b> → + <b class=\"hl\">았</b> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">갔어요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 가요=present, 갈 거예요=future, 가고 있어요=progressive.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Place + <b class=\"hl\">에 가다</b> (갔어요) = \"went to a place\" — 공원에 갔어요!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-6] Listening — 내일 뭐 해요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the best reply.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('내일 뭐 해요?')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  \n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u8q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>내일 영화를 봐요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ tomorrow → future</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>어제 영화를 봤어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ yesterday → past</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>저는 학생이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ </span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>네, 좋아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ </span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u8q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">내일</b> = tomorrow → the answer talks about the <b class=\"hl\">future</b>. \"내일 뭐 해요?\" → <span class=\"pt-ko\">내일 영화를 봐요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Option 2 is about <b class=\"hl\">어제</b> (yesterday/past) — wrong day!</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">내일</b>=future, <b class=\"hl\">오늘</b>=present, <b class=\"hl\">어제</b>=past — match the time word to the verb ending.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-7] Reading — 안 + past meaning</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  \n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">어제 아침을 안 먹었어요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u8q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>I didn't eat breakfast.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 안 + past = didn't</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>I ate breakfast.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ positive</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>I will eat breakfast.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ future</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>I am eating breakfast.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ progressive</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u8q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">안 먹었어요</span> = <b class=\"hl\">didn&#39;t eat</b> (<span class=\"pt-ko\">안</span> + past <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹었어요</span>).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Note <b class=\"hl\">어제</b> (yesterday) — it confirms the action is over, in the past.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">안</b> means NOT, put right before the verb — whether present or past.</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-8] Listening — Choose the past tense you hear</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what you hear.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('드라마를 봤어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  \n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u8q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>드라마를 봤어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ past (watched)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>드라마를 봐요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ present</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>드라마를 볼 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ future</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>드라마를 안 봐요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ negative present</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u8q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard the past form <span class=\"pt-ko\">봤어요</span> (saw/watched). <span class=\"pt-ko\">보다</span> → stem <span class=\"pt-ko\">보</span> ends in <b class=\"hl\">ㅗ</b> → + <b class=\"hl\">았</b> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">봤어요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 봐요=present, 볼 거예요=future, 안 봐요=negative present.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Bright <b class=\"hl\">ㅗ</b> gets <b class=\"hl\">았</b> just like ㅏ — 보다 → 봤어요!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-9] Reading — 감동했어요 meaning</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  \n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우는 노래를 듣고 정말 감동했어요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u8q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>He was deeply moved.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 감동하다 = moved</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>He was having fun.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 재미있다</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>He didn't listen to music.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ negative</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>He went to the bank.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 'will go' / wrong place</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u8q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">감동하다</span> = to be moved / touched → <span class=\"pt-ko\">감동했어요</span> = <b class=\"hl\">was moved</b>. \"Listening to the song, he was deeply moved.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 재미있다=fun, didn&#39;t listen=negative, went to the bank=different verb.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Feelings use tense too: <b class=\"hl\">감동했어요</b>, <b class=\"hl\">재미있었어요</b> — all past!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"practice","html":"<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8-10] Listening — 어디에 갔어요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the correct place + past.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('어제 어디에 갔어요? 시장에 갔어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  \n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u8q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>시장에 갔어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ market + went (past)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>시장에 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ present</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>은행에 갈 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ future</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u8q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>공원이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 이다 (is), not 가다</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u8q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Question <span class=\"pt-ko\">어디에 갔어요?</span> = \"Where did you go?\" → answer <span class=\"pt-ko\">시장에 갔어요</span> = I went to the <b class=\"hl\">market</b> (시장).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 가요=present, 은행에 갈 거예요=future, 공원이에요=is a park (no 가다).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Place + <b class=\"hl\">에 갔어요</b> = \"went to\" — 시장에, 공원에, 은행에!</div></div></div>\n</div>"},{"cls":"culture","html":"<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Diary Writing Challenge</h3>\n    <p>Idols write diaries too! Write about your day using the <b>past tense</b>.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ \"오늘 한국어를 공부했어요. 노래를 들었어요. 정말 재미있었어요!\" — Complete a 3-sentence diary!</div>\n  </div>\n\n</div>"}]}];